window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126 Desperate Search","paragraphs":["\"Who said anything about a divorce?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face went dark. He figured Serena had told him that, and he wasn’t about to say so out loud.","\"Serena’s situation is handled, Mr. Crawford. You can go.\"","\"I know what to say for her. That’s all I came for.\"","\"Jordan.\"","Jordan walked him to the elevator.","Vincent rode down annoyed, and underneath that, sorry for Serena. The man had ended a four year bond for her and still wouldn’t say the word out loud. Anybody could see where that goes.","He texted his associate from the lobby. Confirm the date.","Screenshots came back inside two minutes. Council registry and Bureau of Vital Records, both of them. Bond dissolution, finalized last Thursday.","There was nothing to argue with.","So Hale genuinely didn’t know.","--","Upstairs, Alpha Sebastian had exactly one thing in his head.","Find Eira.","The company was stabilized. Serena was out. For the first time in three days he had an hour to himself, and he was going to use it to explain.","He grabbed his coat and went down to the garage. Didn’t take Jordan. Didn’t call his driver.","He drove to the Thorne estate and barely slowed at the gate. Two guards got in front of the car. One of them had his phone out and was already dialing.","Martin came down the drive and waved them off.","\"Mr. Hale.\" The estate manager’s voice could have frozen the fountain. \"You want to spend another night in a holding room, that’s your business. Don’t do it on our property.\"","\"I just want to see her.\" Alpha Sebastian got out and looked past him at the house, at the windows, at the lawn. \"I know she’s here. She doesn’t have anywhere else to go.\"","Martin’s expression changed slightly at that. Alpha Sebastian didn’t catch it.","\"Let me talk to her. Ten minutes. I’ll explain all of it. Serena, everything.\"","\"What is there to explain?\" Martin didn’t move. \"It’s in writing, Mr. Hale. Four years of it. There’s no version of that story that comes out clean.\"","\"There are things I can only say to her.\"","Footsteps on the gravel behind him.","Beatrice Thorne came around the car and looked at him the way you look at a stain on a rug.","\"Things you can only say to her,\" she said. \"Or things you can’t say in front of anybody else?\"","Alpha Sebastian straightened up. \"Beatrice.\"","\"Don’t. I’m her family. You and I have no relationship.\"","She stopped about six feet away.","\"You know what’s impressive about you, Mr. Hale? Four years. Four years and that girl never once caught on.\"","\"Mrs. Thorne—\"","\"She gave you every dollar she had. Never bought herself anything. Never asked for anything. And you took that money and you put it in a car and a condo and whatever was in those boxes from the jeweler.\" Her voice stayed flat, which made it worse. \"Meanwhile she had to explain a nine hundred dollar charge to your mother.\"","\"What I sent Serena every month was an investment.\"","He’d practiced that one. It sounded thin out loud.","Beatrice actually laughed.","\"An investment.\" She let it hang. \"Then why didn’t you invest in your wife? \"","Alpha Sebastian didn’t answer.","He didn’t have one.","It had never crossed his mind. She didn’t have a job. She stayed home. He’d thought that was the arrangement. He’d thought that was fine.","\"I need to see her.\"","\"You don’t get to need things from her anymore.\" Beatrice’s chin came up. \"The world moved, Mr. Hale, and you’re standing in the same spot. You want to see her? Keep dreaming. Though I doubt she’s in your dreams. I imagine somebody else has that slot.\"","He took it. He didn’t argue. He couldn’t.","\"Please.\" His voice came out rough. \"We were married four years. I’m asking for one conversation.\"","His eyes had gone red.","Beatrice didn’t blink.","\"One conversation. You had fourteen hundred days of conversations. If you’d wanted her once in any of them, if you’d changed your mind one single time, you would not be standing in my driveway.\"","\"You did this.\"","\"And no, you’re not seeing her.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at the house.","He didn’t believe it. Not really. Eira had spent four years telling him she trusted him, that Serena was just a friend, that she wasn’t the jealous type. People don’t turn that off.","He turned toward the front door and shouted her name.","\"Call it in,\" Beatrice said to Martin. She was done.","Martin took out his phone.","\"EIRA.\" Louder. \"Just come out. Let me explain.\"","Nothing moved in any window.","Security was coming anyway, so he ran for it. He got a shoulder past Martin and went straight up the steps.","\"Mr. Hale, that’s trespassing—\"","\"Let him,\" Beatrice said.","Martin stopped where he was.","Alpha Sebastian went down the hall throwing doors open. Empty. Empty. Empty.","He kept saying her name and it kept coming back off the walls.","She wasn’t in any of them.","Then he pushed open a bedroom door and stopped.","There was a gray hoodie hanging on a wooden coat rack by the window.","He crossed the room and took it down. He knew this hoodie. It came in a set of two. She’d shown him the listing on her phone one night, sort of sideways, the way she asked for things, and he’d said sure, buy it.","His had stayed folded in a drawer for four years. He’d never once put it on.","Hers was pilled at the cuffs and gone soft in the wash.","His hand closed around it.","Then he started tearing the room apart.","The balcony. Nothing. The bathroom. Nothing. He pulled the curtains back like she’d be standing behind them.","He left the closet for last.","When he opened it, it was full. Coats, sweaters, slacks, three dresses, everything in cool quiet colors, and every single piece of it was something she would look right in. Somebody had thought about her for a long time to put that closet together.","Alpha Sebastian stood there and didn’t move.","The closet at home was full too. It was full of his suits. Her things had ended up on a rod in the guest room and he could not now remember who moved them there.","Martin was in the doorway.","\"Don’t handle Dr. Crawford’s things.\" His voice was very even. \"Mrs. Thorne and I picked out every piece in there ourselves. You had her in four year old sweaters and somebody else’s coats. The rest of us aren’t going to sit and watch that.\"","Alpha Sebastian shut the closet door and turned around.","\"I’m going to do better. Starting now.\"","Martin smiled with the bottom half of his face.","Too late. She doesn’t need you for that anymore.","\"She isn’t here, Mr. Hale. I’m going to have to walk you out.\"","He didn’t buy it. He went through the rest of it anyway. The hall, both sitting rooms, the kitchen, the garden, all the way down to the tree line.","She wasn’t there.","He finally stopped on the lawn, out of breath, and looked back at the two of them standing by the steps.","He came up the drive slowly.","\"Mrs. Thorne. Please. Just tell me where she is.\"","\"You spent four years keeping things from that girl.\" Beatrice didn’t raise her voice at all. \"You’ll manage to find one person on your own.\"","She turned and nodded at Martin, and the gate rolled shut about a foot from Alpha Sebastian’s chest.","He stood there a while.","Then he took out his phone and called Jordan.","\"Find out where she’s living.\"","Jordan didn’t answer right away.","\"Alpha, I’d advise against it. With her clearance, pulling her address or her movements gets flagged the same day. Not by her. By the Bureau.\" A pause. \"People have gone in front of a judge for less.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","He still hadn’t caught up to it. Somewhere in the last three days, the woman who used to crouch down in the entryway to tie his shoes had become a person he was not allowed to look for.","Fine.","She was his mate. Four years. Nothing on a screen at the Council office changed that.","She’d come around."]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127 An Uninvited Guest","paragraphs":["\"Alpha, if she’s not at the house and she’s not at the Thorne place, that’s three options.\" Jordan came through the car speakers. \"A hotel, somebody’s guest room, or she went home.\"","\"She only goes back to the home at Thanksgiving and Christmas. And she’s running the follow-on with Sterling now.\" Alpha Sebastian didn’t have to think about it. \"She’s not leaving Palo Alto.\"","Hotels or a friend, then.","He put Jordan on the hotels. Every decent one in the city plus the two out by the airport.","The friend he’d take himself. There was only one. Lila Sterling was the only person Eira had spent real time with in two years, and it occurred to him, going through the gate, that he had never once asked what the two of them did together.","\"One more thing.\" He thought about Martin standing in that doorway. He thought about the closet. Fine. He could do that too. \"Call the personal shoppers downtown. Give them her measurements and have them start pulling things. Cool colors. You make the calls yourself.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","Behind him, the gate was already rolling shut.","Martin watched the taillights from the upstairs window until they turned onto the road, then came back down the hall.","\"He’s gone.\"","Beatrice hadn’t moved from the chair by the lamp.","\"Don’t tell her he was here.\" She turned a page. \"She’d go meet him just to keep him off our lawn. You know she would.\"","--","Number Nine, Southridge Estates","Eira and Lila had buried the dining table in takeout. Thai, a pizza, and a rotisserie chicken neither of them could explain. Lila had the champagne open. They were thirty seconds from eating when the doorbell went.","Lila checked the screen by the entry.","Her brother.","Hard pass. She killed the feed.","He rang again. She killed it again.","Then her phone lit up.","\"Lila. Open the door.\"","She nearly dropped it. \"How do you even know it’s me?\"","\"Now.\"","She hung up, scowling. Because Eira wouldn’t leave anybody standing on a porch, that’s how. And because their mom had told him at breakfast where Lila was spending her night.","The door opened.","Alpha Killian’s hand came up to flick his sister in the forehead. Lila had seen that coming since she was nine and was already behind Eira.","Eira was the one who’d opened the door.","So his hand hung there, a foot from her face, fingers half curled.","She looked up at him. What.","Behind her, Lila stuck her head out and lifted her chin. Got Eira now. Can’t touch me.","Alpha Killian gave her a look that could strip paint.","Then he put his hand down on top of Eira’s head, ruffled her hair, and walked past her.","Eira didn’t move.","He followed the smell into the dining room and pulled a plate out of her dishwasher.","\"Unbelievable,\" Lila said. \"Guy acts like he pays the mortgage.\"","Eira was still at the door.","He’d patted her head. Last person who did that was Miss Gwen, and Eira was eleven.","She came to the table at her own pace.","\"Mr. Sterling.\"","\"Dr. Crawford.\"","Hers was polite. His had something under it.","She didn’t explain and he didn’t ask. At the signing he hadn’t blinked. He’d known before she said a word, and half the country knew now anyway.","\"What brings you by?\"","\"Yeah, what are you doing here?\" Lila dropped into her chair. \"You came straight from the office. Don’t tell me you drove across town for our chicken.\"","He set a heavy envelope in front of Eira.","\"The gala. Delivering this one myself, Dr. Crawford.\"","She’d figured Miles would drop it off. Or Kate, who’d volunteered twice.","\"Thank you.\" She got up to put it somewhere it wouldn’t get sauce on it.","When she came back her glass was full again.","Lila’s hands went up. \"Wasn’t me.\"","Which left one person.","Alpha Killian tapped his glass against hers.","\"Congratulations, Eira.\"","Not Dr. Crawford this time.","He put away half of it in one pull.","\"Congratulations to you too, Mr. Sterling.\" She drank half of hers.","Lila frowned. \"Killian, she can’t drink. Why are you pouring like that?\"","He knew she couldn’t. He also knew what she was like once she had.","Seven years sitting on who she was, four more sitting on everything else. She’d earned an hour off.","Last time she got drunk she stopped being careful. Talked like a regular person with things that hurt and nowhere to put them.","Champagne is still alcohol. Half a glass and her face went warm. She touched the back of her hand to her cheek.","Lila shot her brother a look. Nice going.","Alpha Killian looked at his sister, still glaring at him across the table.","\"Eat your food.\"","Lila got two bites in before her phone went off like a fire alarm.","Dez, her floor manager. Her brother knew about the bar. Everybody knew about the bar. She still took it by the window with her back turned.","\"He’s making a scene?\"","\"Wants the owner. Says he’s not leaving till he gets the owner.\"","\"Twenty minutes.\"","She came back to the table and both of them said it at the same time.","\"What happened?\"","Lila looked at one, then the other. When did you two start doing that.","\"Nothing. Something I’ve got to go handle.\" She hugged Eira quick and said into her ear, \"Throw him out. Soon.\"","Then she got in her brother’s face and dropped her voice. \"You try one thing while she’s like this and you’re not my brother. You’re a guy with a restraining order.\"","She made a fist about it.","Alpha Killian didn’t look up. \"Trouble at the bar?\"","\"NO.\" She grabbed her bag and was gone.","\"Don’t scare her,\" Eira said.","\"You two are close.\" Flat.","He says that like a husband.","\"We’re friends.\" She went back to her food. Small bites, slow, the way she did everything.","\"And what are we?\"","\"Business partners.\"","Alpha Killian didn’t say anything.","Right. Why’d he ask.","He picked up his glass and finished it.","Eira didn’t know the first thing about how any of this worked. He emptied his, so she emptied hers.","He stopped. Then the corner of his mouth went up.","Fine. He’d let business partners slide. For now.","It hit her faster than she planned on.","The room tipped. Her fork slid out of her hand and went off the table, and she leaned down after it, straight into the table edge.","Alpha Killian was up before it landed. Her forehead came down soft into his palm.","His knuckles took the edge instead. Hard. He breathed in through his teeth.","His sleeve caught the soup on the way. The bowl went over and started running toward her side.","He came around, got an arm under her, and lifted her clear of it.","Eira made a sound she hadn’t planned on. Her hands came up flat on his shoulders.","She was sitting on his forearm, head tipped down, still working out how she got there.","\"Any of it get you?\"","He turned to look.","Their noses brushed.","Champagne on both of them. Nobody was breathing separately anymore.","Alpha Killian swallowed."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128 Caught in the Act","paragraphs":["Eira’s brain was running about two seconds behind. She blinked, took her time with it, and finally got out a quiet \"No.\"","Soup was still coming off the table edge and hitting the floor in fat drops.","Another second and it would have gone straight into her lap. Alpha Killian was aware of that.","\"Mr. Sterling.\"","He turned his head toward her and made a low sound in his throat. \"Mm.\"","Their noses touched again. She flinched like she’d caught a static shock.","\"You can put me down.\"","Barely a whisper, and it came with champagne on it.","Champagne had never once done anything to Alpha Killian. Champagne on her breath, six inches from his face, was a completely different product.","He put her down slower than the situation called for.","He drank half a glass of water to get his head straight, and when he turned back around she was standing at the table with a box of tissues, blotting up soup.","Of course she was. Thirty seconds alone and she was cleaning.","He caught her wrist. \"Stop.\"","\"It’s a mess. Somebody has to wipe it.\" Her words were coming out slower now, and she was swaying a little where she stood.","He stepped in and closed his hand around her wrist properly. It was nothing. He could feel every bone in it.","He loosened his grip, because he was going to bruise her.","Eira registered that one hand was out of commission and reached for the tissues with the other one.","Alpha Killian exhaled through his nose, pulled his tie off for the second time that night, and tied both her wrists together. Then he walked her, wobbling, over to the couch and sat her down in it.","He got out his phone.","\"Mrs. Jones. Number Nine, Southridge Estates.\"","He hung up, dropped the phone on the coffee table, and looked down at her.","She was sitting perfectly still, staring at nothing about four feet in front of her, gone somewhere else entirely.","\"Eira?\"","Nothing.","He reached over.","She lunged and bit him.","\"Ow—\"","His hand had already had a full day. Split knuckles from the table, and now teeth in the meat of his thumb.","Small teeth. Sharp ones.","The corner of his mouth went up anyway. He tried to pull his hand back.","She held on like it was the best thing she’d eaten all night, working her jaw slowly, absolutely not letting go.","Then she mumbled something into his hand.","\"...funnel cake...\"","\"What?\" He leaned in closer. \"Say that again.\"","Which is exactly when Mrs. Jones came through the front door.","She stopped two steps inside and took in the scene. The two of them on the couch. His hand in her mouth. Her wrists tied with his tie.","\"Oh—\"","Mrs. Jones turned right back around and started apologizing to the wall.","Every book she’d ever read said walking in on your employer at a moment like this got you shouted at.","\"Mrs. Jones.\"","Here we go.","\"Clean up the dining room.\"","\"Alpha?\" She turned around carefully.","And that was when she got the actual picture. Dr. Crawford’s teeth were still clamped down on Mr. Sterling’s hand.","[Well. That’s not romantic at all.]","Alpha. Are you even trying.","Alpha Killian caught the exact shade of judgment in her face, took a slow breath, and looked at her.","\"Mrs. Jones.\"","\"Yes Alpha. Right away Alpha.\" She hustled toward the dining room, head turned the whole way.","From over there she watched the coldest man in Sterling territory go down on one knee in front of Dr. Crawford and say, low, \"That’s enough. Let go.\"","And not pull his hand back even an inch.","Mrs. Jones got her phone out, took one photo, and sent it to Luna Seraphina.","[Luna. You are not going to believe this. There’s progress.]","She looked up again.","He had two fingers under Dr. Crawford’s chin now, tipping her head back until she let go.","Minimal progress, she added.","Then she put the phone away and got to work.","By the time the dining room was done, he was wiping the back of his hand with a napkin. There was a clean half circle of teeth marks on it.","Dr. Crawford had gone sideways into the couch cushions, out cold.","\"All set, Alpha.\"","Alpha Killian nodded once. \"You’re staying here from now on. Meals, groceries, whatever she needs.\"","\"Yes Alpha.\" Mrs. Jones came to attention like somebody had called her rank.","Alpha Killian’s mother was a warm, gracious, thoroughly civilized woman. He had never understood how she managed to collect a household staff composed entirely of lunatics.","Or why she kept assigning them to him.","He looked at Eira, folded into the couch with his tie still loose around her wrists. Her forehead was creased even asleep.","She didn’t look comfortable anywhere.","\"She doesn’t do housework.\"","\"Not while I’m here, Alpha. Not a plate, not a load of laundry.\"","\"If she picks up a dish towel, you’re fired.\"","Mrs. Jones gave him a thumbs up.","\"She can’t sleep down here, though. She’ll wake up sick.\" She said it with her whole face. \"You’ll have to carry her up, Alpha.\"","\"Go do your job.\"","Alpha Killian carried her up expecting to put her in the primary bedroom.","That room was empty. Bed made, nothing on the nightstand, nothing in the closet. Nobody had been in there since the house was furnished.","She’d been sleeping in the guest room.","Miles had already run the deed. The house was in Dr. Thorne’s name.","Alpha Killian stood there a second with her weight on his arm.","Then he took her into the guest room and laid her down and pulled the blanket up.","\"Sebastian.\"","She said it in her sleep, barely.","Alpha Killian’s jaw set.","She started to say something else, and he put his hand over her mouth.","\"If you don’t have anything better than that,\" he said, low, \"don’t talk.\"","He pulled the blanket up over her head.","Then, about a second later, he pulled it back down so she could breathe.","He turned off the lamp and went out.","The door hadn’t finished closing when she said it again, and this time it came out clear.","\"Sebastian. Go to hell.\"","--","RELAX","That was the name of Lila’s bar. One word, no punctuation, very much her.","She came in to find Dez apologizing to a guy who couldn’t stand up straight.","Dez peeled off and met her halfway.","\"What are we dealing with?\"","\"He walked into one of the servers and put his own drink down his shirt. Now he says she did it on purpose. We apologized twice. He wants the owner.\"","Lila went over.","The guy squinted at her. \"You’re the owner? You’re a kid. Somebody’s messing with me.\"","\"Not messing with you, sir. I’ll cover the shirt, and your tab tonight is on us.\"","She could tell he’d come in looking for something to be mad about. She also knew her people hadn’t done anything.","The bar sat two blocks off campus and ran on grad students. Cheaper to make it go away than to make it a story.","The guy blinked at her.","\"Wait. Really?\" He looked around the room. \"Then buy the whole bar a round. On me.\"","\"Done.\"","Lila hadn’t opened RELAX to make money. She’d wanted somewhere to sit that wasn’t a club and wasn’t sketchy, and it turned out a lot of other people wanted the same thing.","The man sat back down, still working on being angry, and couldn’t get there.","Handled.","She headed out to the lot.","[What if Killian actually tries something while she’s like that.]","Girl code beats blood.","She got in the car and pulled onto the street.","Across the road, a Bentley’s headlights came on.","Alpha Sebastian was in the back.","\"Follow her.\""]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129 When the Name Stops Working","paragraphs":["At the Winthrop residence, the silence was one sharp word away from breaking.","Alpha Victor had just returned from the hospital. He sat pale but alert in his favorite leather chair while Robert and Jennifer stood across from Serena, both exhausted and furious.","Jennifer spoke first.","\"How did you think any of this was okay?\" Her voice shook. \"You nearly destroyed your career and dragged Grandpa’s reputation into a federal investigation.\"","\"But I didn’t leak anything.\" Serena crossed her arms. \"If I had actually touched the core data, would I be standing here?\"","Jennifer stared at her.","Robert looked ready to put his fist through the wall.","The moment Serena felt cornered, she turned to Alpha Victor.","\"Grandpa...\" She lowered her eyes. \"I’m sorry. I know I messed up.\"","Robert’s jaw tightened. Of course. Serena still ran to Alpha Victor whenever things went south.","She had grown up in his house after he convinced Robert and Jennifer that he could give her better opportunities and put her closer to the center of Winthrop Pack politics. Serena had chosen him without hesitation.","Grandpa has more power than you. He can do more for me.","Her parents had hoped Alpha Victor would turn her ambition into something useful.","Instead, he had turned it into entitlement.","Serena lifted her chin. \"I grew up with Grandpa. If anyone gets to lecture me, it’s him.\"","Robert let out a humorless laugh. \"You’re not twelve anymore.\"","\"You’re out of the Sovereign Processor Initiative,\" he continued. \"Silix Institute won’t take you back. Your mother and I are taking you home to Arcata.\"","\"No.\" Serena answered too fast. \"I’m not going to Arcata.\"","\"She isn’t going anywhere,\" Alpha Victor said. \"Arcata is too small for her.\"","\"Dad,\" Jennifer said sharply.","Robert stared at him. \"You’ve spoiled her rotten.\"","Alpha Victor’s eyes went cold. \"I raised her. I’ll deal with her. You two don’t get to walk in here and pretend you’re suddenly in charge.\"","Robert’s face darkened. Jennifer looked away, hurt flashing across her face.","Serena relaxed a little. Alpha Victor was still protecting her. He was the Alpha of Winthrop Pack, and his word still carried more weight than anyone else’s in the house.","Robert forced himself to stay calm.","\"Fine. Then tell us what happens next. Serena has been released, but the investigation isn’t over. The federal case can still expand. If the Pack Council gets involved, every major research network could blacklist her. What are you going to do?\"","Alpha Victor tapped the armrest once.","Then he looked at Serena.","\"How close are you to Vincent Crawford?\"","Serena’s eyes flickered. She understood immediately.","The Crawfords were a powerful Pack with money, lawyers, political connections, and influence inside the Pack Council. Vincent was a lawyer. If he agreed to help, he might keep Serena’s name out of the worst of the fallout.","\"Vincent has always been good to me,\" she said carefully. \"He usually helps when I ask. I’m close with his sister, Lainey, too.\"","Alpha Victor watched her for a moment. Serena kept her expression steady. He could always tell when she was overselling something.","\"Set up a meeting. I want to speak with Vincent.\"","\"Of course, Grandpa.\"","Her smile faded almost at once.","Alpha Victor noticed. \"What now?\"","\"Silix is done with me.\" Serena pressed her lips together. \"I can’t get back in.\"","\"Silix isn’t the only research institute in California.\"","\"But it’s the best.\" Her voice sharpened. \"You were the one who taught me to aim for the top.\"","Alpha Victor studied her. \"Do you have what it takes to work at the top?\"","Serena froze.","\"Grandpa!\"","\"What?\" Alpha Victor said. \"You pushed your way into a federal project, did none of the real work, claimed credit you hadn’t earned, and expected everyone to applaud. That’s not ambition. That’s entitlement in expensive clothes.\"","Serena’s eyes filled with tears.","For once, she had no answer.","Alpha Victor waved her off. \"Keep your head down. No interviews. No social media. Don’t call friends who will sell your story to reporters. Stay quiet until this blows over.\"","Serena nodded reluctantly.","Alpha Victor’s expression hardened.","\"There’s one more thing.\"","Her stomach dropped. \"What?\"","\"You and Sebastian Hale. Explain.\"","The room went still.","Robert turned toward Alpha Victor. \"What did you just say?\"","Alpha Victor kept his eyes on Serena.","\"I had someone look into it. Sebastian is married to Eira. Did you know that?\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around her phone.","She could lie to her parents. Alpha Victor was different. He had raised her and knew every pause, every change in her voice, every excuse she used to avoid the truth.","\"I...\" She swallowed. \"I knew.\"","Robert exploded.","\"You got involved with a married Alpha?\"","He took a step forward, but Jennifer caught his arm.","She looked at Serena, her face pale. \"Is it true?\"","\"Mom, you don’t know the whole story.\" Serena’s voice rose, wounded and defensive. \"Sebastian doesn’t love Eira. He never did. He married her because he was angry with me. He wanted me to come back.\"","She lifted her chin.","\"And I did. He’s going to dissolve the bond and divorce her.\"","Robert stared at her.","\"You should have waited until the formal mate separation was complete,\" he said through clenched teeth. \"Instead, you played the other woman while his bond with Eira was still registered with the Pack Council.\"","Serena’s expression twisted.","\"And the money?\" Robert continued. \"You took three hundred thousand dollars from him every month, didn’t you? He was still legally and formally bonded to Eira. Did you ever stop to think about what that money could mean in a separation settlement?\"","\"Sebastian gave it to me.\" Serena’s voice cracked with irritation. \"He never complained. Grandpa never complained. Why are you acting like I robbed a bank?\"","Jennifer flinched.","Robert looked at his daughter as if he barely recognized her.","She hadn’t made one mistake. She had built her entire life around believing she was entitled to whatever she wanted.","Alpha Victor rubbed his temple. \"I would’ve warned you if it would’ve changed anything. It wouldn’t have. Now the question is whether Sebastian will actually divorce Eira. If he does, Hale Pack and Hale Group will pay for it.\"","Serena went quiet.","She wasn’t sure anymore.","Sebastian used to come running after one call. One tear, one reminder of the past, and he was hers again. But lately, his attention kept drifting toward Eira. His temper flared whenever Eira’s name came up. Even Serena’s old tricks had stopped working.","Jennifer saw the doubt on her face.","\"If he loves you so much, why hasn’t he called since your release?\"","Serena’s phone sat silent in her hand. Her messages to Sebastian showed Delivered. Nothing else.","\"He’s dealing with the bid,\" she said. \"Once he gets Hale Group under control, he’ll come.\"","Nobody believed her.","A moment later, the butler entered with two investigators, their Silix Institute badges clearly visible.","\"Dr.Victor Winthrop,\" one said, \"you need to come with us. We’re investigating unauthorized access attempts, personnel recommendations, and your role in the Sovereign Processor Initiative.\"","Serena went white.","Alpha Victor rose slowly. For once, the Winthrop name didn’t make the room fall silent.","It only made the silence worse."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130 The Face He Couldn’t Place","paragraphs":["Alpha Victor wasn’t taken away in handcuffs, but the Silix investigators waiting at the door made one thing clear. This was no courtesy interview.","Robert and Jennifer watched him leave without saying a word. Blaming Serena wouldn’t help now. Victor was old, proud, and used to his Alpha status opening every door. A prolonged investigation would damage his reputation with Silix, the Pack Council, and the entire Winthrop Pack.","They needed favors. Serena knew it.","She texted Vincent Crawford first.","Then she messaged Alpha Sebastian, carefully framing everything as a sacrifice she had made for him, Hale Pack, and the future they were supposed to share. She never asked him to come.","She only left him with enough guilt to make ignoring her difficult.","Serena had always believed guilt was just love with a leash.","That evening, she invited Vincent to a revolving restaurant above downtown. The city glittered beyond the windows, all glass towers, headlights, and fading California light.","She had dressed for an old memory.","A backless silver dress. A white faux-fur wrap. Red lips and blonde waves over one shoulder.","It was almost the same look she had worn the night they met. He had never forgotten.","When Serena approached, her floral scent reached him first.","Vincent stood. \"Serena.\"","He pulled out her chair.","\"Thanks, Vincent.\" She slipped off the wrap and sat. \"I’m sorry it took me so long to thank you properly. Grandpa got dragged into this because of me, and his health took a hit.\"","\"How is Alpha Victor?\"","\"He came home this morning. Physically, he’s fine.\" She gave him a small smile as dinner arrived. \"Let’s eat before it gets cold.\"","She started cutting her steak. Vincent silently traded plates with her. Her steak was already cut into neat pieces.","Serena looked up.","\"Take mine,\" he said. \"I’ll handle yours.\"","Her smile softened. \"You keep this up and your future mate is going to be spoiled rotten.\"","\"Haven’t found her yet.\"","He watched her take a bite and felt a quiet satisfaction he didn’t bother to hide.","Then Alpha Sebastian’s name crossed his mind, followed by Eira’s.","He already knew Alpha Sebastian and Eira had filed their Two Mate Bond Dissolution certificates. He kept that to himself.","\"Have you seen Sebastian since you were released?\"","Serena’s knife stopped. \"Why?\"","\"So he hasn’t checked on you.\"","\"He’s busy.\"","\"Busy chasing Eira, from what I hear.\"","Her appetite vanished.","\"Vincent.\"","He raised a hand. \"All right. I’m dropping it.\"","They ate in silence for a few minutes.","When the dessert menus arrived, Serena lifted her wineglass.","\"I really do owe you. You made calls and helped keep things from getting worse. I don’t even know how to repay you.\"","\"You helped me once. I returned the favor.\"","\"Once?\" She gave him a sad smile. \"I stopped you from drinking one bad cocktail. You’ve helped me more times than I can count.\"","Vincent took a sip of wine.","Serena waited until he set the glass down before making her move.","\"Grandpa wants you to come to dinner at the Winthrop residence. He’d like to thank you in person.\"","Vincent looked genuinely surprised.","Victor still led the Winthrop Pack, and an invitation from him was never just dinner. It was a formal gesture between Packs, usually followed by a favor, a negotiation, or both.","\"When?\"","Serena didn’t answer right away. \"How long are you staying in Palo Alto?\"","\"Why?\"","\"Grandpa may not be free for a few days. I’m not sure how long.\" Her voice softened. \"Something happened.\"","Vincent’s expression sharpened. \"What happened?\"","Serena looked down and blinked hard. \"He told me this morning to invite you. Then Silix sent investigators to the house and asked him to come in for questioning.\"","Vincent’s face settled into a lawyer’s calm.","He didn’t need the details. If Silix was looking into unauthorized access, personnel recommendations, and influence over the Sovereign Processor Initiative, Victor’s position as Winthrop Alpha would not protect him for long. Pack rank opened doors. It did not erase a paper trail.","Serena’s eyes filled with tears. \"This is all my fault. If I were as talented as Eira, no one would be tearing me apart on every research board and Pack channel in California.\"","\"Eira is good,\" Vincent said. \"That doesn’t make you useless. You have your own work.\"","Serena lowered her gaze. \"I just hate that I can’t help Grandpa.\"","Vincent watched her for a moment, then flagged down the waiter. A few minutes later, a chocolate dessert arrived.","\"Don’t spiral,\" he said. \"I’ll deal with it.\"","Serena looked up. \"You will?\"","\"Victor invited me. I’m not going to ignore a senior Alpha’s hospitality. I’ll stay in Palo Alto until I speak with him.\"","\"What about your cases?\"","\"I can work remotely. No hearings this week.\"","Relief flashed through her eyes, quickly covered by a fragile smile. \"Thank you, Vincent.\"","\"That’s enough thank-yous for one night.\"","They finished dinner without further trouble.","By the time Vincent paid and they reached the elevator, Serena had almost convinced herself the evening had gone exactly as planned.","The doors opened.","Lila stood inside with one arm linked through Eira ’s. She had been laughing about the restaurant’s seafood tower, but her smile vanished the moment she saw Serena.","\"Well, this is awkward,\" Lila said. \"Or maybe just bad timing.\"","Serena’s expression froze.","Eira stood quietly beside Lila, sea-gold waves falling over her shoulders, rimless glasses catching the light. She wore nothing flashy, but there was a clean, untouchable composure to her that made Serena’s sequins suddenly feel loud.","Lila’s gaze slid over Serena with open disgust.","\"Didn’t expect to run into Sebastian’s favorite side quest tonight.\"","Serena’s face went white.","Vincent’s jaw tightened.","\"Miss Sterling,\" Serena snapped, \"try having a little class.\"","Lila smiled sweetly. \"I would, but you used up the room’s supply pretending you weren’t sleeping with a bonded Alpha.\"","Vincent stepped forward, his eyes on Lila but his attention strangely pulled toward Eira.","\"Careful,\" he said. \"Accusations like that can get ugly fast.\"","Lila arched a brow. \"So can the truth. Funny how that works.\"","Eira didn’t speak.","She only looked at Vincent once, calm and unreadable.","And Vincent, who had seen her in news clips and photos, felt that odd sense of recognition hit him harder in person.","It wasn’t just familiarity.","It was specific.","Her eyes. The bridge of her nose. The composed, almost scholarly restraint behind her glasses.","She looked like his father, Henry Crawford, in the old family photographs.","Not exactly.","But close enough to make Vincent’s pulse hesitate."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131 Eira Strikes First","paragraphs":["People looked alike sometimes. That was all it was.","The same eyes. The same mouth. The same stubborn line of the jaw.","A coincidence. Nothing more.","Vincent had spent thirty years believing Alpha Henry was his father. He’d grown up hearing how Alpha Henry had walked away from the Pack Council, choosing Luna Clara, his family, and his pack instead.","His father had given up everything for his mother.","Vincent wasn’t about to rewrite thirty years of his life because a stranger happened to look familiar.","So he looked away.","\"Miss Crawford,\" he said, turning to Eira, \"are you going to rein in your friend, or is this how the Sterling Pack handles itself in public?\"","Eira glanced at Lila.","Lila raised her brows. \"What? I didn’t say anything that wasn’t true.\"","\"She asked a fair question,\" Eira said.","Vincent’s jaw tightened. \"You and Sebastian have already—\"","He stopped. Serena stood beside him. Even he knew better than to discuss Eira’s dissolved mate bond in front of the woman who had helped cause it.","Eira understood anyway.","So Vincent knew about the Two Mate Bond Dissolution Certificates.","Good. That saved her some time.","She turned to Serena. \"You were involved with Sebastian while our mate bond was still registered.\"","Serena’s face flushed.","Eira’s mouth curved faintly. \"But congratulations in advance. I’ll send flowers when Hale Pack announces its new Luna.\"","She paused, her gaze sweeping over Serena.","\"Not that I’d ever want to be part of a pack like that—or tied to wolves like you.\"","The insult landed because everyone understood what she had left unsaid. If Eira had refused to dissolve the bond, Serena would still be waiting in hotel rooms and borrowed apartments. Even now, Alpha Sebastian had not claimed her publicly.","Vincent frowned. \"Miss Crawford, maybe don’t kick someone while she’s down.\"","Eira looked at him. \"Do you say that in court too, Counselor? ’Your Honor, my client committed fraud, but let’s all be nice about it?’\"","Lila snorted.","Vincent’s expression darkened.","\"Funny,\" Eira continued. \"I thought lawyers preferred facts.\"","\"Speaking of facts,\" Lila said, folding her arms, \"does your father know you’re in Palo Alto defending a woman accused of sleeping with a bonded Alpha, pulling strings at Silix, and reaching for classified research she had no clearance to access?\"","Serena stiffened.","The first two accusations were ugly, but familiar. Pack scandals lived in group chats, private clubs, and council gossip for weeks.","The last one was different.","Vincent’s voice dropped. \"Careful. Throwing around words like classified and leak without proof can get expensive.\"","\"So can subpoenas.\" Lila smiled. \"But sure. Let’s pretend Silix sent investigators to the Winthrop residence for the complimentary coffee.\"","Serena’s eyes filled with tears. \"Why are you being so cruel?\"","\"Because I’m allergic to homewreckers.\"","Vincent’s gaze shifted to Eira.","\"Does Luna Seraphina know her daughter is running around with a wolfless Omega who has no Pack blood behind her?\"","The air in the lobby changed.","In old Pack society, bloodline meant protection, territory, inheritance, and political leverage. An orphaned, wolfless Omega had none of it. Elite Packs might offer charity. They did not offer a seat at the table—or a place in the family—unless they expected something in return.","Lila stepped forward, but Eira caught her wrist.","Eira faced Vincent instead.","\"For a man with two living parents,\" she said calmly, \"that was a remarkably fatherless thing to say.\"","Lila choked back a laugh.","Vincent’s face hardened. \"Sharp tongue.\"","\"Better than an empty head.\"","Serena’s nails dug into her clutch.","Eira had changed. The quiet Luna who once swallowed every insult in Hale Tower was gone. In her place stood someone polished, untouchable, and completely unafraid.","\"Does Sebastian know you’ve become this nasty?\" Serena asked.","Eira didn’t blink. \"Does Sebastian know you’re having dinner with another man, or are you still auditioning for Luna?\"","Serena’s eyes filled again. This time, the tears looked softer—carefully arranged to make Vincent step in.","He did.","\"Enough, Miss Crawford.\"","Lila was already pulling out her phone.","\"Hi, Mom.\"","Eira turned toward her.","Absolutely not.","Lila tapped the speaker.","Seraphina’s voice came through. \"Lila? Aren’t you and Eira at dinner?\"","\"We just got here.\" Lila kept her eyes on Vincent. \"Quick question. Would you be embarrassed if one of my friends grew up without parents?\"","A beat of silence followed.","Then Seraphina’s voice turned cold. \"Lila Sterling. Who taught you to say something that ugly?\"","Lila smiled at Vincent. \"You’re right. That was awful. Sorry, Mom.\"","\"Apologize properly.\"","\"I will.\"","\"And come home after dinner.\"","Lila winced. \"Love you too.\"","She ended the call.","Vincent looked as if he had just bitten into broken glass.","Serena’s fragile act cracked. Once Luna Seraphina had been dragged into the exchange, there was no graceful way to keep fighting. Vincent gave Eira one last unreadable look before following Serena into the elevator.","The doors slid shut.","Lila exhaled sharply. \"God, what a dumpster fire. We came for dinner and got a full biohazard event.\"","Eira’s lips twitched. \"Are you okay?\"","Lila’s phone pinged.","Mom: Lila Sterling, come straight home after dinner.","Lila stared at the screen. \"She used my full name. That’s never good.\"","Eira glanced at her. \"Still okay?\"","\"Totally.\" Lila was already typing. \"I have a secret weapon.\"","She opened Killian’s chat and fired off a quick summary of the elevator disaster—Vincent’s insult, Serena’s fake tears, and Seraphina’s reaction.","Then she added:You’re my actual brother. Save me. Come home with me tonight.","--","Outside the restaurant, Serena tried to regain control.","\"Don’t let Lila get to you,\" she told Vincent. \"Sterling money has clearly gone to her head. And Eira’s been acting different ever since she started running with them.\"","\"Borrowed power,\" Vincent said coldly.","Serena lowered her eyes. \"I’m used to it.\"","\"That’s the problem. You shouldn’t be.\"","Before she could answer, a Bentley pulled up to the curb.","Serena recognized it immediately.","Alpha Sebastian.","Her heart jumped. For one awful second, she wondered whether he had seen her leave dinner with Vincent.","Then hope took over.","He had come for her.","\"Vincent, I’m sorry,\" she said quickly. \"Sebastian’s here. You should head home.\"","Vincent glanced at the Bentley, his expression tightening. \"Go.\"","\"I’ll text you.\"","She crossed the sidewalk, her steps growing lighter with every stride.","But Alpha Sebastian hadn’t come for her.","The night before, he had seen Lila drive through the gates of Southridge Estates—somewhere his own car had been turned away. He had left a driver watching the entrance. When the driver reported that Eira had left in Lila’s car, Alpha Sebastian had come straight to the restaurant.","He stayed downstairs instead of going up. The last thing he needed was Lila Sterling turning his private business into Pack gossip.","\"Alpha,\" the driver said carefully, \"Miss Winthrop is coming over.\"","\"Serena?\" Alpha Sebastian looked up.","Before he could react, the driver opened the door, and Serena slipped inside.","\"Sebastian.\" She moved close and took his hands. \"You finally had time for me. I’m freezing. Warm me up.\"","Her wrist knocked against the wallet in his hand. It fell to the floor.","Alpha Sebastian bent down, but Serena reached it first.","The wallet had fallen open.","Inside the clear pocket was a plain ring.","Eira’s ring.","Serena’s gaze dropped to Alpha Sebastian’s left hand.","He was wearing the band he had once stopped wearing—the wedding band from his marriage to Eira.","He hadn’t worn it when Serena first returned to California. Back then, he had treated his mate bond to Eira like meaningless Pack.","Now he carried Eira’s ring in his wallet and wore his own as if he were mourning the marriage he had thrown away.","Serena’s smile slowly faded."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132 The House Was Never Hers","paragraphs":["Before Alpha Sebastian could close the wallet, Serena reached for the ring. He caught her wrist.","\"What are you doing?\"\"What are you doing?\"","Serena blinked up at him, green eyes wide with practiced innocence. \"Trying it on. Isn’t that what rings are for?\"","\"It’s not yours.\"","The answer came too fast. Too sharp.","Her smile thinned. \"Then whose is it?\"","Alpha Sebastian took the ring from her fingers and slipped it back into the wallet.","\"If you want jewelry, I’ll buy you something better.\"","Serena went still. \"It’s for Eira, isn’t it?\"","\"It’s Eira’s.\"","The Bentley suddenly felt too small.","\"The ring is Eira’s. You’re still hung up on Eira.\" Her voice cracked. \"Is that where we are now? She’s useful, she’s all over the news, and suddenly she belongs beside you?\"","\"This has nothing to do with the Sovereign Processor Initiative.\"","\"Then what does it have to do with?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"It was our wedding ring. Mine and Eira’s.\"","The words sounded more final than he intended.","Serena gave a brittle laugh. \"And what am I supposed to do with that? You’ll buy me cars, apartments, and jewelry—but not a place beside you?\"","He said nothing.","\"Will you give me a wedding ring, Sebastian?\"","There it was. No more games.","\"Anything but that.\"","Serena recoiled as if he had slapped her.","She had received his money, protection, research funding, and connections. Everything except the title, the bond, and the public commitment she wanted.","\"Don’t do this to me.\" She threw her arms around him. \"Please, Sebastian. Don’t leave me.\"","His hand lifted out of habit, then stopped. He let it fall.","\"I have something to handle,\" he said, looking toward the restaurant entrance. \"We’ll talk later.\"","\"My grandpa will be fine.\" Serena changed tactics at once. \"I’m already calling people. He has former students everywhere. Silix can ask questions, but no one’s going to crucify him over a misunderstanding.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze sharpened. \"I told you not to cross that line.\"","\"I was trying to help you win.\" She softened her voice. \"Your parents wanted Hale Pack to secure that chip advantage too. Your father asked about the Initiative more than once. Are you blaming them as well?\"","That struck a nerve.","Alpha Roger had pushed for the deal.Luna Margaret had encouraged it. Everyone had wanted the same shortcut—energy independence, military contracts, and a stronger seat before the Pack Council.","Alpha Sebastian exhaled. \"The bid is gone. The investigation is still active. As for Alpha Victor, I’ll deal with him myself.\"","Then he checked the time. Eira and Lila would be coming down soon.","He removed Serena’s hands from his coat. \"My driver will take you home.\"","\"You’re not coming with me?\"","\"I said I have something to handle.\"","He stepped out, closed the door, and gave the driver a short nod.","The Bentley pulled away before Serena could stop it.","\"Let me out!\" she snapped, slapping the window.","\"Alpha Sebastian instructed me to take you home, Miss Winthrop.\"","\"I said let me out!\"","The privacy screen rose with a soft hum.","Serena kicked the back of the seat and immediately regretted it. Pain shot through her foot.","She knew exactly what Alpha Sebastian was handling.","Eira.","--","Back at the restaurant, Alpha Sebastian returned to the lobby and took a seat facing the elevators. He didn’t order a drink or check his phone. He simply waited.","When the doors opened, Lila stepped out with her arm linked through Eira’s, still laughing.","\"Admit it,\" Lila said. \"This place was worth the price. Next time, I’m dragging Mom here. She’ll pretend she’s too classy for truffle fries and then eat half the basket.\"","Eira smiled faintly—then spotted Alpha Sebastian.","He reached them before she could take three steps.","\"Eira.\"","For a second, he forgot what he had planned to say.","She looked nothing like the quiet Luna who had once managed Hale Pack with grocery lists, staff schedules, and his mother’s endless complaints in hand.","This Eira belonged in boardrooms and federal briefings. She stood beside people Alpha Sebastian had spent years trying to impress.","He had missed all of it.","Worse, he had never bothered to look.","Lila immediately stepped between them. \"Nope. Whatever you’re selling, we’re not buying.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked past her. \"Eira, I’ve been trying to reach you for two days. You blocked my number.\"","\"Maybe take the hint,\" Lila said.","Eira’s gaze stayed on him. \"Shouldn’t you be checking on your $300,000-a-month investment?\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","So she knew.","Lila gave a humorless laugh. \"Classic move. Keep the mistress on the payroll, then come crawling back to the wife when she blows up a federal project. What a strategy.\"","People in the lobby began to glance over.","Alpha Sebastian lowered his voice. \"Can we not do this here? Come home with me. We need to talk.\"","\"Home?\" Eira repeated. \"I don’t have a home with you.\"","\"It’s your house.\" He followed as she walked away. \"I signed it over to you. Hale apartment is yours.\"","Eira didn’t slow down.","\"That house was always in your name.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped.","A cold realization hit him. He remembered the paperwork, the signature, and the way Eira had remained perfectly calm while he signed whatever she had placed in front of him.","His stomach dropped.","\"Then what the hell did you have me sign?\""]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133 Rot Draws Flies","paragraphs":["Eira didn’t answer.","By the time Alpha Sebastian recovered, Eira and Lila had reached the curb. A black Cullinan waited there with the engine running.","Alpha Killian got out, nudged Lila into the back seat, and turned to Eira.\"Get in.\"","Lila rubbed the back of her head after bumping it on the doorframe. \"Seriously? I’m your sister.\"","\"Get in,\" Alpha Killian repeated.","\"Fine. No family drama. We unite against the common enemy.\" She looked at Eira. \"Come on.\"","Eira slid into the car without looking back. She had no interest in standing on a sidewalk while Alpha Sebastian served up another round of empty promises.","\"Eira!\" Alpha Sebastian hurried after her.","Alpha Killian stepped between them.","\"Alpha Sebastian. Have some self-respect.\"","Alpha Sebastian let out a bitter laugh. \"That’s rich coming from you. Every time Eira and I have a disagreement, you show up like you’ve been waiting around the corner. What are you trying to do, Alpha Killian? Play the other man?\"","\"Relax.\" Alpha Killian’s eyes swept over him. \"Eira doesn’t send me three hundred thousand dollars a month. She hasn’t bought me a penthouse, a million dollars’ worth of jewelry, or a two-million-dollar car.\"","He paused.","\"So no, I’m not the other man. Don’t project your own mess onto me.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s mouth opened.","Nothing came out.","The money. The jewelry. The car. The penthouse.","Every gift Serena had accepted suddenly looked less like generosity and more like evidence.","Alpha Killian got back into the Cullinan and shut the door.","The SUV pulled away, leaving Alpha Sebastian alone on the curb.","He stood there for a moment before kicking a concrete planter hard enough to scatter soil across the sidewalk.","Lila leaned out the window and gave him a thumbs-up. \"Very classy, Hale. Mom was wrong, though. You’re definitely capable of talking.\"","Alpha Killian shot her a look sharp enough to end the joke.","Lila ducked back inside.","Alpha Killian turned to Eira. \"Did he put a tracker on you?\"","Eira had wondered the same thing. She had left Hale Pack, blocked every number connected to it, and upgraded her security after the Sovereign Processor Initiative became public. Alpha Sebastian shouldn’t have been able to follow her.","If he had been watching her, he had made a serious mistake. She was no longer just a former Hale Pack Luna anymore. She was connected to classified federal research. The Bureau wouldn’t treat unauthorized surveillance as a private Pack dispute.","\"I ran into Serena at the restaurant,\" Eira said. \"Lila and I both saw her.\"","\"Serena wouldn’t have told him,\" Alpha Killian said.","\"Vincent Crawford would.\" Lila leaned forward from the back seat. \"Your favorite legal nemesis. I told you about him.\"","The Reeds and Crawfords had known each other for years. Their families crossed paths at Pack functions and holiday gatherings in Washington, D.C.","Luna Seraphina had once tried to set Alpha Killian up with Lainey Crawford.","It had gone badly.","Alpha Killian had avoided Lainey Crawford, Fiona Carter, and every other eligible woman with the dedication of a man escaping a federal subpoena. He had even claimed to be blind when Lainey invited him for a walk.","Vincent had never forgiven him for embarrassing Lainey in front of both families.","Since then, the two men had traded insults at every opportunity. Their mutual friends had learned one basic rule:","Never seat Alpha Killian and Vincent together at a Pack function.","\"Vincent is representing Serena now?\" Alpha Killian asked. \"Is that legal work, or does he just want to get into her case?\"","He had never known Vincent to work for free.","Lila tilted her head. \"Serena’s got game. Two men circling her at once.\"","\"Rot attracts flies,\" Eira said.","The siblings turned to stare at her.","Lila grinned. \"Okay. I like this version of you.\"","\"What?\" Eira glanced between them. \"It’s just an old saying.\"","\"You’ve got a sharp mouth,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Use it more often.\"","\"I’ll second that,\" Lila said.","Eira gave a small hum of agreement.","She had once loved the entire Hale Pack because she had loved Alpha Sebastian. Love me, love my people.","But after four years of being taken for granted, there was nothing left to love.","--","The Cullinan passed through the gates of Southridge Estates and stopped outside Number Nine. Eira crossed the wide front lawn and found Mrs. Jones waiting at the door with a bright smile.","\"Miss Eira, welcome home.\"","\"Mrs. Jones?\" Eira unlocked the door with her fingerprint. \"What are you doing here?\"","Mrs. Jones folded her hands. \"Alpha Killian asked me to take care of the house and make sure you’re eating properly.\"","Eira stared at her. \"Killian sent you?\"","Mrs. Jones nodded. \"He said you shouldn’t have to handle everything alone while you’re working on the joint project.\"","That sounded exactly like something Alpha Killian would arrange without asking permission.","\"I appreciate it, but I can take care of myself. You should go back.\"","Mrs. Jones’ smile faltered. \"Please don’t send me away, Miss Eira. Alpha Killian said if I couldn’t work here, I’d lose my position with the Sterling household.\"","Eira frowned. \"Then I’ll cover your salary.\"","\"He’d still dismiss me. And...\" Mrs. Jones hesitated, then sighed. \"My mother’s in assisted living, and my son’s in college. I really need this job.\"","The guilt trip was almost too polished.","Then Mrs. Jones added, \"Alpha Killian said he only wants you to have enough time to focus on the project. He thinks the work is important.\"","That part sounded sincere.","Eira studied her for a moment before stepping aside. \"Fine. You can stay for now. But I don’t need a full-time babysitter.\"","Mrs. Jones brightened. \"Of course not. Think of me as household support.\"","\"Exactly.\"","\"Absolutely.\"","The moment Eira showed her to the first-floor guest room and closed the door, Mrs. Jones pulled out her phone.","\"Reporting in, Alpha. I’m officially inside.\"","Alpha Killian pinched the bridge of his nose on the other end of the call. \"I sent you there to help her, not spy on her.\"","\"Spy is such an ugly word. I prefer ’keep you updated.’\""]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134 Old Wounds","paragraphs":["The Sterling estate was quiet when Alpha Killian and Lila came through the front door.","Marnie Sterling was in the living room, a mug of tea in hand. She glanced up and smiled.","\"Killian. Twice in one week? Should I be worried?\"","\"Aunt Marnie.\"","\"Congratulations on the contract.\" Her gaze shifted briefly to Lila, then back to him. \"And on Eira Crawford. Beatrice recommended her, didn’t she? She seems to have made quite an impression around here.\"","\"She has.\"","Marnie’s brows lifted at the quick answer, but she let it slide. She reached over and smoothed Lila’s hair.","\"Good night, sweetheart.\"","\"Night, Aunt Marnie.\"","The moment Marnie disappeared down the hall, Lila hooked her hand around Alpha Killian’s arm.","He calmly freed himself.","Alpha Killian crossed the room and took the armchair opposite his mom.","Lila dropped onto the sofa beside Luna Seraphina. \"Mom, before you start, I’d like to present my side of the case.\"","Luna Seraphina’s mouth twitched. \"You have the floor.\"","\"Vincent started it. He asked whether I was embarrassed to be seen with someone who had no family. An orphan.\" Lila’s expression hardened. \"He said it like Eira’s background was some dirty little secret people should whisper about at Pack functions.\"","Luna Seraphina’s face cooled. \"That boy has always had a mouth on him.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"That wasn’t permission to repeat him.\"","Lila’s smile vanished.","Luna Seraphina turned fully toward her. \"You don’t get to throw someone’s pain back at them just because they handed you an opening. You and Killian were taught better than that before either of you could control a first shift.\"","\"Yes, Mom.\"","\"Good.\"","Luna Seraphina gave Lila’s cheek a light pinch, then looked at Alpha Killian.","\"And you? Did you come home to defend your sister?\"","\"He didn’t do anything,\" Lila said. \"Our alliance is officially over.\"","She sprang to her feet and headed for the stairs. \"I’m surrounded by traitors.\"","Alpha Killian waited until she was out of sight before turning to his mother. \"Where’s Dad?\"","\"In the study. He was on a call with your uncle and aunt.\" Luna Seraphina leaned back. \"Rhys graduates soon. He wants to come home and join the Sterling Group.\"","Alpha Julian emerged from the study just then, ending the call as he walked in.","\"Well, look who finally decided to come home.\"","Alpha Killian ignored the greeting and got straight to the point. \"What position does Uncle have in mind for Rhys?\"","Alpha Julian hesitated. \"That’s a conversation for another day.\"","Alpha Killian let the subject drop. If Alpha Julian wanted to keep it in the family for now, pushing him would only make him shut down.","Instead, Alpha Julian changed the subject.","\"I hear Vincent is in Palo Alto. He’s been meeting with half the Pack Council about Victor Winthrop’s situation.\" His gaze settled on Alpha Killian. \"Since when did he become the Winthrops’ hired gun?\"","\"He isn’t,\" Alpha Killian said. \"He’s involved with Serena.\"","\"Involved how?\" Seraphina gave him a look. \"That’s a little more than a lawyer-client relationship.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Alpha Julian studied his son. \"Vincent doesn’t get personally involved unless there’s something in it for him.\"","\"Serena’s smart,\" Alpha Julian added. \"She could’ve gone far if she’d ever had to earn anything on her own.\"","\"She never had to,\" Seraphina said. \"Victor opened every door for her. All she had to do was walk through and take the credit.\"","\"And now Vincent is cleaning up after her.\"Alpha Julian shook his head.\"That’s a lousy investment.\"","\"Good,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Maybe he’ll finally lose something.\"","Alpha Julian glanced at him. \"You’re still holding a grudge against Vincent?\"","\"I’m not holding anything.\"","\"Killian.\"","\"He started it.\"","Luna Seraphina let out a long-suffering sigh. \"You two have been taking cheap shots at each other since high school. You’re grown men now. Try acting like it.\"","\"Start with him.\"","\"I said both of you.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw flexed. He turned toward the window.","Luna Seraphina watched him for a moment before continuing. \"Vincent didn’t become Lainey’s personal bodyguard for no reason.\"","Alpha Killian looked back at her. \"What happened?\"","\"There was an incident when she was a baby. At the hospital.\"","His expression sharpened, but he said nothing.","\"Henry had just been assigned to the Crawford Pack’s northwestern border to deal with a serious security breach. The territory was remote and difficult, and he could barely make it home once a year. Clara couldn’t stand being separated from him, so she insisted on joining him.\"","Alpha Julian leaned back against the sofa. \"A romantic gesture with questionable medical timing, I’m guessing.\"","Luna Seraphina gave him a warning look.","\"What? I said I was guessing.\"","\"It wasn’t long before Clara became pregnant,\" Luna Seraphina continued. \"Henry wanted to send her home as soon as he found out. He was worried about the conditions there and didn’t want her going through the pregnancy without proper medical care.\"","\"But Clara refused.\"","\"She wouldn’t leave him alone at the border. Lainey was born more than a month early. The delivery was difficult, and Clara didn’t recover well afterward.\"","Luna Seraphina’s voice softened.","\"She would pick Lainey up and hold her, then panic and set her down as if she couldn’t bear to touch her. A moment later, the baby would start crying, and Clara would scramble across the floor to get her back. She’d clutch Lainey so tightly that Henry sometimes had to pry her arms away.\"","Alpha Killian’s face tightened.","\"Once, Clara lost her grip and threw her,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"If Vincent hadn’t caught Lainey, she could have suffered serious injuries.\"","The room fell silent.","\"For a long time after that, Henry and Vincent wouldn’t let Clara be alone with Lainey. They weren’t punishing her. They were afraid she might hurt the baby without realizing what she was doing.\"","\"And that was when Henry asked you for help?\" Alpha Julian asked.","\"Yes.\" Luna Seraphina nodded. \"He came to me privately and asked if I knew a specialist who could help Clara. That was when I learned what had happened at the hospital.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes narrowed. \"What happened?\"","\"Lainey had nearly gone missing shortly after she was born. She was found in the end, but the incident left Clara badly shaken.\"","\"With treatment, Clara eventually got better.\" Luna Seraphina’s smile was faint and sad. \"But after that, she never let Lainey out of her sight. Not for a second. \"","Her smile was faint and sad.","\"Lainey became the center of the Crawford family. Vincent took his job as her big brother very seriously.\"","She looked directly at Alpha Killian.","\"So when you rejected Lainey in front of both families, Vincent didn’t see an awkward moment. He saw history repeating itself—another person hurting his little sister.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression went blank again. \"Lainey knew I wasn’t interested.\"","\"She knew you didn’t return her feelings,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"That doesn’t mean she deserved to be humiliated in front of everyone.\"","\"I didn’t humiliate her.\"","\"I don’t need Vincent’s permission to make my own choices,\" Alpha Killian added.","\"No one said you did,\" Alpha Julian replied. \"But let’s turn this around. If some idiot kept making Lila feel small, would you shrug and say, ’Not my problem’?\"","Alpha Killian opened his mouth.","Then he noticed Lila leaning over the second-floor railing.","She was staring down at him, her eyes narrowed to slits.","Alpha Killian took one look at her and wisely shut his mouth."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135 The Hardest Assignment","paragraphs":["When Alpha Sebastian got home, Jordan was overseeing a team from one of the city’s top boutiques. Garment bags covered the floor, and employees were filling the walk-in closet with clothes, shoes, and handbags.","Alpha Sebastian stopped in the doorway.","The closet had once held nothing but his suits. Now there was no sign that Eira had ever kept anything there.","Jordan noticed his expression and smiled to himself. So the Alpha had finally decided to spoil his Luna. He had cleared out his old clothes and ordered her a whole new wardrobe.","Knowing Eira, she would have worn the same coat for another five years if no one had stopped her.","\"We’re out of space,\" Jordan told the staff. \"Put the rest in the guest room.\"","That had been Alpha Sebastian’s idea. He had ordered the room turned into a proper dressing room for Eira.","Jordan turned as Alpha Sebastian approached.","\"Everything’s here,\" he said. \"The clothes and shoes are sorted by season, just like you asked.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked around the apartment.","For the first time, he noticed how cramped the three-bedroom place felt. Eira had lived here with him for four years and had never complained about the lack of space. She had never asked for a bigger home, either.","\"Start looking at houses,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I want a few options by the end of the week.\"","\"Sure.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at him. \"Why is this place still in my name?\"","Jordan blinked. \"I thought you transferred it to Luna Eira.\"","\"I did.\"","\"Then she must have handled the paperwork herself. She never mentioned it to me.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. \"Check tomorrow. I want a full report on every property and account still tied to my name.\"","\"Will do.\"","Jordan reached into his pocket and held out a Porsche key fob.","\"The car you ordered for Luna Eira arrived this afternoon.\"","\"Good.\"","Alpha Sebastian took the keys.","It was not exactly a celebration gift for landing the contract, but it would make a decent peace offering.","Four years did not fall apart overnight.","He could fix this. He always did.","\"Jordan, get me a few new phone numbers.\"","\"Burners?\"","\"Numbers Eira won’t recognize.\"","She had blocked Alpha Sebastian and every member of his family. If she would not take his calls, he would find another way to reach her.","Jordan gave him a doubtful look, then nodded. \"I’ll see what I can do.\"","\"And keep an eye on Lila Sterling.\"","Jordan understood what Alpha Sebastian was asking. He also knew it was the kind of request that could create a serious legal problem.","Still, he nodded. \"I’ll handle it.\"","By the time the boutique staff finished, the apartment looked more like a showroom than a home.","Alpha Sebastian dismissed the crew and took a shower. He had barely stretched out on the bed when his phone lit up.","Finn: Hey, do you know Eira?","Alpha Sebastian remembered the look on Finn’s face the first time he saw her. The kid had been completely smitten.","His jaw tightened.","He started typing.","[She’s my wife.]","Before he could send it, another message came through.","Finn: Do you have her number? Can you send it to me?","Alpha Sebastian stared at the screen.","His thumb hovered over the keyboard. Then he deleted the message, opened Eira’s contact, and forwarded her number instead.","A reply came almost at once.","Finn: Seriously? Thanks, man. I owe you one.","A moment later, Finn sent Eira a connection request.","Then he waited.","A minute passed.Then another.Nothing.","It was late. Eira was probably asleep. She would accept it in the morning.","Finn set his phone on the nightstand and fell asleep with a smile on his face.","--","The next morning, Finn woke to a notification on his phone.","Eira had accepted his connection request.","He was out of bed in seconds and carried that good mood through breakfast.","Fiona watched him over her coffee. \"What’s with the grin?\"","\"What grin?\"","\"That ridiculous one on your face.\"","Finn glanced at his phone, trying and failing to hide his smile. \"You wouldn’t understand.\"","\"You met someone.\"","\"How did you know?\"","His twin dimples appeared.","Fiona studied her younger brother. He was handsome, cheerful, and about as subtle as a golden retriever carrying a stolen sock.","\"Let me guess. She’s older.\"","Finn’s grin widened.","\"Finn.\"","\"What? Women our age aren’t exactly lining up for the golden-retriever routine.\"","\"Women our age have standards.\"","\"Older women appreciate charm.\"","\"Older women appreciate a man who knows when to stop talking.\"","Finn slipped his phone into his pocket. \"I’m heading to Carter Group.\"","\"Try not to fall in love before lunch.\"","\"No promises.\"","In the back of the town car, Finn opened Eira’s contact and sent her a message.","Finn: Hey, it’s Finn. We met at the restaurant. Do you remember me?","Eira saw the message while getting ready to leave.","Eira: I remember you.","Finn: Good. I was worried I’d made a terrible first impression.","Before Eira could answer, her phone rang.","Professor Davies.","\"Eira, can you stop by the Silix Institute this morning?\"","\"Sure. I’m on my way.\"","\"Perfect. I’ll meet you upstairs.\"","The call ended.","Another message from Finn appeared.","Finn: Are you busy today?","Finn: Maybe we could grab coffee sometime?","Eira: I’m swamped today. I’ll catch up with you later.","She muted the conversation and put her phone away.","A cab took her straight to the Silix Institute.","The guard at the entrance stood as soon as she walked in.","\"Good morning, Dr. Crawford.\"","\"Morning.\"","She gave him a warm smile and continued through the lobby.","\"Morning, Doctor.\"","\"Congratulations.\"","\"Welcome back.\"","Eira returned the greetings with a nod or a smile. She knew most of the staff were only trying to be polite, but she also knew how quickly people started whispering when someone acted as if they were above everyone else.","From the second-floor skybridge, Professor Davies and Claire watched her cross the lobby.","Claire shook her head. \"She’s going to greet every person in the building, isn’t she?\"","\"Probably.\"","\"If she didn’t, half the staff would decide the attention had gone to her head.\"","Davies smiled. \"Let’s get her to the new office before someone else claims it.\"","They reached the office just as Eira arrived.","Davies opened the door. \"Here you go.\"","Eira stepped inside. The office was larger than she expected, with floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the Institute’s central courtyard.","\"This is mine?\"","\"Unless you hate it.\"","\"I don’t.\"","\"Good. Then let’s get through the paperwork.\"","He placed several folders on the desk.","\"The federal housing office approved a secure residence for you. Your professorship has also been submitted for formal review.\"","Eira picked up the first folder.","\"10 Ashford Lane,\" Davies said. \"The property has cleared the initial security review. Once the final inspection is complete, you can move in.\"","Eira closed the folder. \"I’ll move as soon as I can.\"","\"That’s probably wise.\"","Davies pushed another stack of folders toward her.","\"These are recruitment offers. Universities from New York to California are competing for you. They’re offering research grants, relocation packages, lab space, and tuition benefits for dependents.\"","Eira stared at the stack. \"They’re offering all that?\"","\"They’re trying to outbid each other.\"","\"I see.\"","\"Don’t rush into anything,\" Davies said. \"Take a few days. Have Susan review the contracts before you sign.\"","\"I will.\"","Claire had been quiet until then. She pulled out a chair and sat down.","Eira looked at her. \"What is it?\"","\"There’s an update on Dr. Winthrop.\"","Eira’s expression turned serious. \"What kind of update?\"","\"The investigation is moving forward. The court has also scheduled his sentencing hearing.\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136 Reclaiming What Was Hers","paragraphs":["\"That fast?\" Eira asked. She was still surprised by how quickly the investigation had moved.","Professor Davies adjusted his glasses. \"Nothing’s official yet. But the Institute has seen plenty of important visitors these past few days. Some even flew in from D.C.\"","Eira understood. The case had attracted attention from people who mattered.","Claire folded her arms. \"And the computer Serena accessed wasn’t assigned to Eira. Professor Davies and I both used it for research records and internal reports.\"","\"That makes Serena’s case harder to prove,\" Davies said. \"She may avoid serious criminal charges. Winthrop is in a worse position, but unless prosecutors can prove fraud or a major federal violation, he probably won’t lose everything.\"","\"Serena’s reputation won’t recover,\" Claire said. \"No reputable institute will want her.\"","Eira nodded. \"That’s about what I expected.\"","The law might not be able to do much to Serena.","But Alpha Sebastian had used their marital money to buy her an apartment, a car, and expensive jewelry. That was a separate issue, and one Eira had almost forgotten to address.","She pulled out her phone and called Susan.","\"Susan, it’s Eira.\"","\"Dr. Crawford. I saw the news. What do you need?\"","\"Sebastian and I are divorced. The judgment is final. He spent a large amount of money on Serena while we were married. Can I still pursue those assets?\"","Susan paused. \"If he used marital funds and failed to disclose the transfers during the divorce, possibly. We would need to review your final financial disclosures and trace where the money came from.\"","\"I’ll gather everything I have and send it over. I’ll leave the legal side to you.\"","\"You got it. Once I’ve reviewed the records, I’ll tell you what we can do.\"","Eira ended the call.","--","The Hale Estate.","Isabella’s routine had barely changed, but Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret had spent the morning sitting in uneasy silence.","Alpha Roger regretted letting Eira talk him into filing for divorce. He still had no idea how to break the news to Alpha Sebastian.","Luna Margaret had a different problem.","For four years, Eira had lived off Alpha Sebastian’s money. Now that she had a career and money of her own, Luna Margaret couldn’t understand why she wasn’t putting any of that success back into the Hale family.","As far as Luna Margaret was concerned, Serena was still the better match.","\"Mom, Dad, I’m heading out.\"","Isabella came downstairs with her purse over one shoulder.","\"Where are you going?\" Luna Margaret called.","The front door slammed before Isabella answered.","A Bentley Continental GT waited at the curb. Serena was behind the wheel, already lowering the passenger window.","\"Bella, get in.\"","Isabella climbed inside. \"We’re picking up my stuff from my brother’s place, then heading to the stables?\"","\"Yep.\"","Serena pulled away from the curb.","\"Thanks for coming with me,\" she said. \"I didn’t want to bother Sebastian. He’s been buried in work lately. I still feel bad that I couldn’t help him land that contract.\"","\"Seriously?\" Isabella scoffed. \"That wasn’t your fault. Eira had what we needed and refused to help. She basically handed the deal to Sterling.\"","That was the story the Hales knew.","Carter Group had buried the real reasons behind the failed bid, especially Alpha Sebastian’s involvement with Serena. By the time the truth had turned into office gossip, none of it had reached the Hale family.","To them, Serena was still the sweet, beautiful woman who had always stood by Alpha Sebastian.","When they reached Alpha Sebastian’s building, Serena glanced at Isabella.","\"You can get us upstairs, right?\"","\"Obviously. I know the access code.\"","As they walked inside, Isabella shook her head.","\"Eira is so damn cheap. My brother’s a CEO, and she still has him living in a place like this. She controlled every dollar he spent. I swear, he completely lost his mind.\"","Serena said nothing.She kept her eyes on the elevator doors.","They pulled into the garage. Alpha Sebastian had two assigned parking spaces.","One was empty.","A car sat in the other beneath a dust cover.","Isabella stopped. \"What the hell is that?\"","She grabbed the edge of the cover and pulled it back.","Serena froze.","A Volcano Gray Porsche Panamera sat underneath.","Her fingers tightened around her purse.","For months, she had been an authorized user on Alpha Sebastian’s main credit-card account. Just yesterday, she had noticed that more than half of the available credit was suddenly gone.","That was why she had come.","Alpha Sebastian had never cared about sports cars.","So why had he suddenly bought one?","And why this particular model?","\"Bella, leave it for now.\" Serena forced a smile and stepped out of the Bentley. \"Let’s go upstairs. We still have the stables.\"","--","At the apartment door, Isabella punched in the access code and let them inside.","The place looked exactly as it always had. Serena made a quick show of checking the living room, then slipped down the hall and opened the door to Alpha Sebastian’s bedroom.","She stopped cold.","Behind the glass closet doors hung rows of women’s clothes. There were so many that they took up half the closet, sharing the space with Alpha Sebastian’s suits and casual clothes.","The last time Serena had been there, the entire closet had belonged to Alpha Sebastian. Eira’s few things had been pushed into one corner.","Serena slid one of the doors open and checked the tags.","Brand-new clothes.","All of them looked expensive.","\"Oh, my God!\" Isabella shouted from the next room.","Serena found her in the guest room.","It had been completely redone. Clothing racks lined the walls, organized by type. Handbags and shoes sat behind glass display doors. The room wasn’t packed with designer pieces, but it had clearly been designed for one person.","This was where Isabella and Serena used to stay when they visited. Even the old pullout couch was gone, replaced by a stylish sofa.","Serena stared at the room, her jaw tightening.","Alpha Sebastian had finally started spending money on Eira.","That thought stung more than it should have.","\"Has Eira lost it?\" Isabella complained. \"She used to pinch every penny, and now she’s blowing through Sebastian’s money like there’s no tomorrow. Does she even know how much this stuff costs?\"","Isabella barely looked at the clothes. Her attention had already locked onto two handbags behind the glass.","Serena noticed the way her eyes lingered on them.","She stepped closer and lowered her voice.\"That one would look great on you.\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137 The Car That Wasn’t Hers","paragraphs":["\"Seriously?\" Isabella rolled her eyes, but she was already reaching for the bag.","She lifted it from the glass case and turned it over in her hands. Small, sleek, and exactly her style.","\"Besides, it came out of my brother’s pocket,\" she said. \"One bag isn’t going to break the bank.\"","Serena smiled. \"It looks great on you.\"","\"I know, right?\"","Isabella slipped the strap over her arm and admired herself in the mirror.","While Isabella was distracted, Serena scanned the shelves. A black gift box was tucked behind the handbags.","She pulled it out.","\"What’s that?\" Isabella asked.","Serena opened the lid.A set of car keys lay inside.","Isabella picked them up. \"Car keys?\"","She turned them over and spotted the Porsche emblem.","\"But my brother already has a car. And we have the family SUV. Why would he buy another one?\"","Her eyes widened.","\"Unless Eira bought it.\"","Serena looked at her. \"Eira drives?\"","Isabella snorted. \"Please. That woman can barely get around town. Whenever we visit the family cemetery, Dad or Sebastian drives her.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around her purse.","If Eira couldn’t drive, the car probably wasn’t for her.","Isabella stared at the keys. Then her face lit up.","\"Wait. You think Sebastian bought it for me?\"","Serena gave her a small smile.","She didn’t need to answer.","\"Oh my God. He did.\" Isabella hugged the keys to her chest. \"My brother bought me a car!\"","\"Why don’t you go see it?\"","\"Hell yes.\"","Isabella hurried toward the garage, with Serena following close behind.","They pulled the cover off together.","A Volcano Gray Porsche Panamera gleamed beneath it.","Isabella stared at the car. \"Okay, I’m not going to lie. I hate the color.\"","\"Take it for a spin before you judge it,\" Serena said.","\"Gladly.\"","Isabella climbed into the driver’s seat, grinning from ear to ear.","\"Try not to miss me.\"","The engine roared. A second later, the Porsche shot out of the garage.","Serena watched it disappear down the road.","Only then did her smile fade.","The car had not been bought for Isabella.","It had been bought for Eira.","Serena had been using Alpha Sebastian’s main credit card for months. The day before, she had noticed that more than half of the available credit was gone.","Now she knew where at least some of that money had gone.","Alpha Sebastian had spent it on Eira.","The thought made Serena’s jaw tighten.","Her phone rang.","Jordan.","She answered at once. \"Is Sebastian looking for me?\"","\"Ms. Winthrop, Sebastian has been tied up all morning. He asked me to contact you about something important. Are you free?\"","\"Right now.\"","\"Perfect. I’ll see you soon.\"","They ended the call.","Serena glanced toward the road. This worked out better than she had expected. She could not take Isabella to the stables anyway. The city’s best riding club was outside town and members-only, and Serena had no way through the gate.","She called Isabella.","Isabella answered on the second ring, sounding thrilled.","\"Bella, Jordan just called. Sebastian needs to discuss something with me, so I have to skip the stables today. Can we take a rain check?\"","\"Seriously? I was looking forward to it.\"","\"I know. But you have a brand-new Porsche waiting for you.\"","\"That’s fair.\" Isabella laughed. \"We’ll go next time.\"","--","Jordan had chosen a café across from Hale Tower. It was quiet enough for a private conversation and close enough for Serena to keep an eye on the building.","\"Ms. Winthrop.\"","He waited until she sat down before taking the chair across from her.","Serena glanced toward Hale Tower. \"We’re five minutes from Sebastian’s office. He couldn’t tell me this himself?\"","\"He’s tied up with the Carter project. Carter’s watching him closely. If the bid falls apart, Alpha Sebastian could be pulled from the project or placed on leave.\"","Her irritation faded. Alpha Sebastian’s position still mattered to her. Without his money and connections, she had no chance of building her own research team.","\"What’s going on?\"","\"Things at home have become complicated,\" Jordan said. \"Alpha Sebastian wants to make sure the situation doesn’t create problems for you.\"","Serena’s eyes narrowed. \"What kind of problems?\"","\"Luna Eira may challenge several payments Alpha Sebastian made during the marriage. The apartment, the car, the jewelry, and the money transferred to your account.\"","\"She can’t just take those things back.\"","\"If the money came from marital assets, she may be able to seek reimbursement. The total value could exceed a hundred million dollars.\"","Serena stared at him. \"So what does Sebastian want me to do?\"","Jordan placed a folder on the table.","\"He wants you to sign an acknowledgment stating that the apartment and the car were part of an investment arrangement, not personal gifts.\"","\"That’s not what they were.\"","\"I know.\"","Her expression hardened. \"So this is a cover story.\"","\"It’s an attempt to put the arrangement in writing before Eira’s attorney starts asking questions. It may help. It may not. Without documentation, you have no protection at all.\"","Serena glanced at the folder but did not open it.","Jordan held out his hand. \"The card first.\"","She pulled Alpha Sebastian’s black card from her purse and dropped it onto the table.","\"Jordan, you know Sebastian loves me.\"","[He used to,] Jordan thought.","He slipped the card into his pocket. \"Sign the agreement.\"","Serena scanned the first page. \"It says I won’t owe him anything if the investment fails.\"","\"That’s the idea.\"","\"And if Eira takes this to court?\"","\"You may still have to answer questions. This only gives us a position to defend.\"","Serena’s pride took a hit, but she signed the agreement and pushed it back to him.","Jordan collected the papers. \"One more thing. The apartment and the car will be described as loans.\"","\"Loans?\" Serena’s voice sharpened.","\"That’s how Alpha Sebastian wants the transactions recorded.\"","She stood, furious. Then she stopped.","\"What about the Porsche he bought for Isabella?\"","Jordan frowned. \"What Porsche?\"","Serena gave him a cold look and walked out.","His phone rang a moment later.","Isabella.","\"Hello, Miss Hale.\"","\"Jordan, the Porsche is insured, right?\" Her voice was small and nervous. \"I had a little accident.\"","Jordan closed his eyes. \"How bad?\"","\"I clipped a curb. The paint’s scratched, and the front bumper is dented.\"","\"And the hood?\"","There was a pause.","\"It’s only a little bent.\"","Jordan pressed two fingers to his temple.","It was going to be a very long day."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138 A Gift Long Overdue","paragraphs":["The Porsche was insured. That was not the problem.","The problem was that Jordan was starting to think about quitting.","He arranged the tow truck and called the repair shop while Isabella followed him around, twisting her hands.","\"Jordan, please don’t tell my brother yet,\" she begged. \"I know the car is mine, but I wrecked it on the first day. He’s going to lose it.\"","Jordan rubbed his forehead.","First Serena. Now Isabella. Somehow, he had to explain all of this to Alpha Sebastian, who was already under enough pressure with Eira refusing to speak to him.","Then Jordan noticed the handbag sitting on the passenger seat. He recognized it immediately.","\"Miss Hale, the car was bought for Luna Eira.\"","Her mouth fell open.","\"So was the handbag,\" Jordan continued. \"You need to tell Alpha yourself. He’s dealing with enough right now.\"","The contract was gone. Eira wanted nothing to do with Alpha Sebastian. Serena was creating new problems by the hour, and his family kept making things worse.","\"Eira?\" Isabella stared at him. \"But she can’t even drive.\"","\"Then she can learn.\" Jordan gave her a flat look. \"There’s nothing strange about a husband buying his wife a car.\"","Isabella’s face flushed.","\"And I’m not covering for you this time,\" he added. \"Once the car is repaired, Alpha Sebastian gets the truth.\"","Alpha Sebastian had two things left on his plate: keeping his position by securing Dr. Shaw’s patent and convincing Eira not to walk away for good.","Everything else could wait.","Even Serena.","Isabella watched Jordan walk away, then looked at the tow truck carrying the Porsche down the street.","Her stomach twisted.","Fine. She would get ahead of the story.","The moment she got home, she went straight to her parents.","\"Mom, Dad, you won’t believe what Alpha Sebastian bought for Eira. A Porsche, a designer handbag, and enough clothes to fill an entire dressing room. He even gave her the guest room.\"","Margaret’s face tightened.","\"He never spends money like that on either of you,\" Isabella continued. \"And now that Eira has money of her own, she’s still draining him dry.\"","That hit a nerve with Margaret.","For four years, Margaret had hated watching Eira decide how Alpha Sebastian’s money was spent. Now Eira was no longer living with him, yet Alpha Sebastian was still throwing money at her.","Isabella saw the look on her mother’s face and pressed harder.","\"I’m telling you, Mom. Eira talked him into all of this. She knows exactly how to get him to open his wallet.\"","\"The nerve,\" Margaret snapped. \"After everything this family has done for her, she still has the nerve to take his money?\"","Alpha Roger frowned. \"Or maybe Sebastian is trying to win her back.\"","Margaret shot him a look. \"After everything we’ve been through with her?\"","Before Alpha Roger could answer, Margaret’s phone rang.","\"Sebastian, Isabella was just telling us about the car...\"","\"Mom, I’m slammed. And keep Isabella out of Eira’s things. I’m not dealing with another mess.\"","Margaret glanced at Isabella.","Alpha Sebastian continued, \"I’m also changing the locks on the house Eira and I shared. From now on, nobody goes in without checking with me first.\"","\"But Sebastian...\"","The call ended.","Margaret stared at her phone.","\"He’s changing the locks.\"","Isabella’s eyes widened. \"What? I only took the Porsche for a test drive. And I only grabbed one bag.\"","Alpha Roger gave her a pointed look.","\"Exactly.\"","Isabella rolled her eyes and said nothing. She was already thinking about which three handbags she’d rotate through first.","Margaret barely heard them.Her expression hardened.","Alpha Sebastian wasn’t spending that kind of money for no reason.","Eira was still pulling his strings.","And Luna Margaret was done sitting back and watching it happen.","\"No,\" she said, rising from her chair. \"I’m going to talk to Eira myself.\"","--","The next morning, Luna Margaret showed up at the front gate of the Silix Institute.","\"I’m here to see Eira Crawford.\"","The security guard looked her over. \"Do you have an appointment?\"","\"No. It’s personal. Tell her Margaret Hale is here. If she won’t see me, I’ll wait right here.\"","The guard glanced at the line of people entering the building. \"Ma’am, you can’t block the entrance.\"","\"Then call her.\"","Clearly eager to move the argument away from the gate, he contacted the front desk.","Eira was in her office that morning.","When the receptionist mentioned the Hale family, she immediately thought of Alpha Sebastian. A second call confirmed that only his mother had come.","Luna Margaret would not leave quietly. Eira decided it was better to deal with her now, before she caused a scene inside the Institute.","Eira had barely reached the lobby when Luna Margaret spotted her and stopped.","Eira’s hair was glossy, her skin clear, and there was color in her face that had been missing for years. She looked healthier than she ever had while living with Alpha Sebastian.","Luna Margaret’s expression darkened.","\"So you finally decided to take care of yourself,\" she said. \"You couldn’t have done that while you were married?\"","Eira kept her voice calm. \"You came here to comment on my appearance?\"","\"Don’t change the subject.\" Luna Margaret stepped closer. \"Why is Sebastian buying you cars, clothes, and designer bags? You agreed to leave the marriage with nothing.\"","So that was what this was about.","\"Those things weren’t for me,\" Eira said. \"They were for Serena.\"","Luna Margaret stared at her. \"Sebastian told Isabella they were yours. He even warned her not to touch them. \"","Eira almost laughed.","\"Four years of marriage, and you lived off my son. Now you’re divorced, and you’re still bleeding him dry. Have you no shame?\"","\"Your son controls his own money,\" Eira said. \"Take it up with him. Aside from the allowance he gave me, I never had access to another cent.\"","\"That’s impossible.\"","\"Is it?\" Eira tilted her head. \"You still don’t know why Sebastian lost the contract, do you?\"","Luna Margaret’s expression shifted.","\"It wasn’t because of his private life,\" Eira continued. \"Carter Group is investigating him for allegedly funneling money to Serena, the outside consultant on the project.\"","\"Funneling money,\" she added. \"In other words, they suspect he may have paid her to influence the bid.\"","Luna Margaret went still.","Eira took out her phone.","\"There’s something you should see. The people directly involved have already seen it. As Sebastian’s mother, you deserve to know what happened too.\"","She called Mrs. Jones.","\"Could you bring a file from my home office? I’ll text you pictures of the documents.\"","\"Of course, Miss Crawford. Where should I meet you?\"","\"At the gazebo in Stone Park, across from the Institute.\"","\"Got it. I’ll be there shortly.\"","Luna Margaret’s eyes narrowed. \"What file?\"","Eira met her gaze.","\"A gift,\" she said. \"One that’s long overdue.\""]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139 The Truth on Paper","paragraphs":["Mrs. Jones found the folder exactly where Eira had told her to look: tucked away in the bottom drawer of Eira’s home office desk.","She picked it up and headed for the door. Halfway down the stairs, the folder slipped. Papers scattered everywhere.","\"Damn it,\" Mrs. Jones muttered, crouching down. She began gathering them, eyes fixed on putting everything back in order.","Then one page caught her eye. A bank statement. Large transfers. Alpha Alpha Sebastian’s name. Serena Winthrop.","She froze. The figures were impossible to miss. She picked up another page. Then another.","By the time she finished, her face was red with anger.","Mrs. Jones placed the papers back in the folder, closed it, and continued to Stone Park. Eira had asked her to deliver the file to Luna Margaret. She hadn’t said what was inside, but now Mrs. Jones understood.","When she reached the gazebo, Luna Margaret looked her up and down. \"And who exactly are you?\"","\"I work for Miss Crawford.\"","\"A housekeeper?\" Luna Margaret sniffed. \"What makes you think you can look down on me?\"","\"You’re right, ma’am. Nothing wrong with being a housekeeper.\" Mrs. Jones straightened. \"But I don’t raise spoiled brats who think the world owes them a living.\"","Luna Margaret’s face darkened. \"Are you calling my son a brute?\"","\"Did I say that?\"","\"Watch your mouth. Say one more thing and I’ll wipe that smirk off your face.\"","Eira stepped forward. The file was what mattered, not a public shouting match.","But Mrs. Jones was already fired up. She planted her hands on her hips and stepped closer until Luna Margaret instinctively took a step back.","\"Before you start making threats, read what your golden boy has been doing with his money.\"","Luna Margaret snatched the folder. \"Fine. Let’s see what garbage you’ve cooked up.\"","She opened it. The first page silenced her.","Her eyes moved across the figures. Confusion. Then her hands began to shake as she flipped through the documents.","\"This is fake,\" she whispered. \"It has to be.\"","But the records were clear. Year after year, Alpha Alpha Sebastian’s money flowed into Serena Winthrop’s accounts. Hundreds of thousands at a time.","\"I think you understand it perfectly,\" Eira said, her voice calm. \"Alpha Sebastian and I were married for four years. He gave me three thousand dollars a month. I paid the rest of our household expenses with my own salary. When Isabella wrecked her car and ended up in the hospital, your family expected me to cover the settlement. How was I supposed to do that on three thousand dollars a month?\"","Luna Margaret’s lips parted, but no words came out.","\"While Serena was overseas, she drained three hundred thousand dollars a month from Alpha Sebastian’s accounts,\" Eira continued. \"The day she came home, he bought her a Bentley. Then he bought her a luxury penthouse.\"","She nodded toward the folder.","\"That penthouse is worth twice the value of your entire neighborhood. Yet you spent four years calling me a gold-digger and accusing me of ruining your son.\"","Eira’s voice remained steady.","\"The truth is, Alpha Sebastian penny-pinched everywhere else just so he could give Serena whatever she wanted. He starved himself, his wife, his parents, and his sister so he’d never have to say no to the woman he really loved.\"","Luna Margaret stared at the documents.","\"The five-figure handbags Serena carried, the designer clothes, the jewelry worth more than most people’s homes. Your son paid for all of it.\"","Eira paused.","\"Alpha Sebastian used to tell me that money should be saved or invested. He kept me on a tight budget, and I accepted it because I knew he loved Serena, not me.\"","Her gaze hardened.","\"But he lied to you too. He let his own family believe I was the one wasting his money. He let you blame me for his choices.\"","The words hit Luna Margaret harder than any insult.","She had adored Serena. Now she was seeing the truth.","Serena had been bleeding Alpha Sebastian dry long before she ever became part of the Hale family. She had not been the devoted woman everyone thought she was. She had been draining his accounts while the family blamed Eira.","\"Serena,\" Luna Margaret whispered. Her breathing grew fast and uneven. \"That little snake...\"","Then her knees gave out.","Eira rushed forward and caught her before she hit the ground. She lowered Luna Margaret carefully onto the bench.","Mrs. Jones pulled out her phone and called 911. \"If she collapses here, Miss Crawford will be dragged into another mess,\" she muttered.","The paramedics arrived within minutes and took Luna Margaret to the nearest hospital.","Eira and Mrs. Jones followed in Mrs. Jones’s car.","Neither of them had expected the truth to affect Luna Margaret so badly.","--","When Luna Margaret came to in her hospital bed, Eira and Mrs. Jones were gone. Her husband and son were the only ones waiting at her bedside, both looking worried.","\"Mom, you’re awake.\" Alpha Sebastian was on his feet the instant her eyes opened. \"What happened? Why’d you collapse?\"","Alpha Roger leaned in too. \"How are you feeling, honey?\"","Luna Margaret thought of the file. Every word Eira had said. The fury clogged her chest all over again, a red haze behind her eyes.","She lifted a trembling finger and pointed at her son.","\"You tell me the truth right now. Where did all your money go these past four years?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s breath caught. Panic flickered through his eyes, quickly replaced by a blank mask.","Alpha Roger frowned. \"Why is that the first thing out of your mouth, Margaret? Wasn’t Eira handling the finances all along?\"","\"The hell she was!\" Luna Margaret’s hand shot up like she meant to slap him, then thought better of it.","Her voice broke with a raw grief that shattered the usual composure of a Pack Luna. \"Tell me. Look me and your father in the eye and tell me. Your salary, your dividends, your investment returns. All of it. Where did it go? Why were you hiding it from us?\"","Alpha Roger read her expression and felt his stomach drop. He turned on his son. \"Are you tangled up in something you shouldn’t be, Sebastian?\"","\"No.\" Alpha Sebastian’s mouth flattened into a hard line.","\"Then what is your mother talking about?\"","Luna Margaret couldn’t hold it back. \"He gave it all to Serena!\"","Her voice was a cracked whisper. \"He couldn’t spend a dime on this family—not on his wife, not on his parents, not on his sister—but he could pour a fortune into some outsider with no name, no ring, no claim to us!\"","She looked at Alpha Sebastian, her voice rising. \"Did you ever buy me jewelry worth six figures? Did you ever buy your father a car that expensive? Did you shower Isabella with designer bags? Do you even own anything valuable yourself?\"","Alpha Sebastian took the tongue-lashing without a word.","Alpha Roger looked at his silent son, then at his wife’s bloodless face. \"Where did you hear all this, Margaret?\"","\"Where did I hear it? I didn’t have to hear anything. Eira threw the proof right in my face.\" Her cheeks still stung from the public humiliation.","\"Eira? You went to see Eira?\" Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped up. All he wanted to know was how his mother had gotten near her.","Luna Margaret’s head was pounding, but her mind was locked on one thing: the money, the betrayal, the shame of it all.","\"Roger, ask your son yourself. Is it true or not? Sebastian, tell your father, am I lying?\""]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140 A Lesson Written in Regret","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian knew there was no hiding it anymore. \"Serena needed support. She was brilliant. I was backing her research.\"","Luna Margaret’s eyes rolled back, and she fainted a second time.","The doctor rushed in. \"No more stress! Whatever this is, take it outside.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared down at his mother, jaw tight. This was exactly the scene he’d tried to avoid. The whole reason he’d lied.","\"Outside. Now.\" Alpha Roger’s voice was low, dangerous.","--","The slap cracked through the hallway.","Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped sideways. His father had held back, but the sting bloomed hot across his cheek.","\"I thought you were tossing her a few grand to keep her happy,\" Alpha Roger said, his voice shaking. \"I didn’t think you’d handed over a goddamn fortune to some outsider. You trying to sink this pack?\"","Alpha Sebastian swallowed, meeting his father’s furious eyes. \"Dad, I was investing in her career. It was a private venture.\"","\"A private venture.\" Alpha Roger’s face went dark as a thundercloud. \"One investment? Your entire net worth? What happened to common sense? Did that girl charm it right out of you?\"","He didn’t buy the \"investment\" line for a second. His son wasn’t stupid. Just played.","No wonder Eira had wanted out. She’d lived four years with a husband funneling their joint future into another woman’s pockets.","Alpha Roger’s chest felt like it was pinned under a boulder. They’d let a good Luna slip through their fingers, chasing a ghost.","\"Some venture. Serena just bought herself a penthouse . Did that come from ’research funds’?\"","Alpha Sebastian had nothing. \"I stopped funding her after she came back.\"","\"Then explain the penthouse. The luxury cars. The designer everything.\" Alpha Roger’s voice sharpened.","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"Your mother’s been making you soup every night because she thinks you’re working too hard. And you repay her by putting her in a hospital bed.\" Alpha Roger’s voice cracked. \"I don’t care about your past with Serena. You paid that debt a hundred times over. If you go crawling back to her, don’t bother calling me your father.\"","\"Dad—\"","\"If you’d given Eira even a fraction of what you threw at that woman, none of this would’ve happened.\" Alpha Roger pressed a hand to his own chest, short of breath.","A damn fine Omega, gone. His son had trashed it all. And Moon Goddess help him, so had he.","\"It won’t happen again,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"From now on, everything goes to Eira. I’ll make it right.\"","[Make it right. ]Alpha Roger nearly laughed. [You’re already divorced, you idiot.]","\"You get your head straight about that girl, and you get it straight today,\" Alpha Roger said. \"You put your energy into your work and into winning Eira back. You hear me?\"","Get Eira back. Patch things up. Remarry. Simple.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw firmed. \"I know. But she won’t see me. And Killian always shows up. I think he wants her.\"","Just saying Killian’s name made his blood run hot. A mated woman, riding around town in another Alpha’s car, brushing him off like he was nobody.","Alpha Roger frowned and waved it off. \"Rich men’s games. He doesn’t want her. He wants the win. Brilliant or not, she’s still an orphan with no Pack bloodline. The Sterlings and the Reeds will never accept her. No Alpha heir brings home a divorced woman.\"","Something about that last part snagged at Alpha Sebastian. [Divorced woman?]","\"Eira wouldn’t divorce me,\" he said. \"And I’d sure as hell never divorce her.\"","Alpha Roger opened his mouth, then closed it. A month ago he’d have believed his son without blinking. Now he just looked at him with a mix of pity and disgust.","\"Focus on her. Understood?\"","\"I know.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice steadied. \"She’s my wife. She’s the only one I should’ve ever been thinking about.\"","Alpha Roger studied his son’s reddened cheek. \"Still sting? Good. Let it teach you something. I don’t care what you and Serena had. You’re done with her.\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded and followed his father back inside. Luna Margaret still hadn’t woken.","Isabella came flying through the door, throwing herself against the bed rail in tears. \"Dad, Sebastian—what happened to Mom?\"","\"Your brother happened,\" Alpha Roger said flatly.","\"Sebastian!\" Isabella whirled on him. \"How could you upset her enough to land her in a hospital?\"","\"Enough.\" Alpha Sebastian looked at his sister, and for once there was no softness in it. \"You’ll wake her.\"","Isabella blinked, thrown. Then her mouth twisted. \"This is about Eira, isn’t it?\"","[Every drama in the last four years always circled back to that woman. Eira, the wrecking ball. Always trying to tear their perfect little family apart.]","Alpha Sebastian didn’t correct her. Their mother had, in fact, collapsed over the truth Eira laid bare.","\"I knew it.\" Isabella’s voice dropped to a hiss. \"That woman won’t rest until she’s burned this whole family down. She’s nothing but a cheap little—\"","\"Isabella.\" Alpha Sebastian’s tone cut like a blade. \"What did I tell you about respecting her? She’s your Luna.\"","\"I don’t want her as Luna!\"","Alpha Sebastian said, each word iron. \"You don’t get a vote. You took her handbag. You took her car and wrecked it. I didn’t make you pay for the damage or apologize, and that was me being generous.\"","Isabella’s mouth fell open.","\"Touch her things or disrespect her again,\" Alpha Sebastian went on, \"and I cut you off. No allowance.\"","Isabella stared at him, stunned into silence."]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141 A Note in the Coat Pocket","paragraphs":["Isabella was ready to keep fighting when Luna Margaret finally stirred.","Alpha Sebastian called out to his mother softly. No response.","He let out a breath, resigned. \"Dad, I won’t stand here and stress her out. I’ll go.\"","He left without another word.","Luna Margaret lay in the hospital bed, staring at the ceiling, tears sliding down her cheeks.","\"Mom, what’s wrong?\" Isabella rarely saw her mother this shattered.","Luna Margaret was too choked with fury to speak. She just kept dabbing at her eyes.","Isabella looked to her father.","Alpha Roger heaved a heavy sigh and gestured. \"Go get your mother some warm water.\"","\"Fine.\" Isabella dragged her feet toward the door.","Alpha Roger sat beside the bed and handed his wife a tissue. \"It’s done. Fuming here won’t undo it. You’ll only make yourself sicker.\"","\"How am I supposed to stay calm?\" Luna Margaret pressed the tissue to her eye.","\"If Sebastian hadn’t wasted pack money on a woman who wasn’t even part of our family, he could have invested in new territory, funded border patrols, or strengthened our alliances. He could have done something useful with it instead of throwing it at an outsider who gave him nothing in return.\"","Isabella heard every word, and her own anger grew.","So it was true. Her mother was furious because Alpha Sebastian had spent so much money on Eira.","Eira had never done anything for the family. She had never bought them a single gift, yet Alpha Sebastian kept spending money on her.","Ungrateful witch.","\"Mom, you’re right, Sebastian never should’ve spent it on—\"","\"Don’t you throw gasoline on this fire.\" Alpha Roger took the water cup from her hand and passed it to his wife.","Isabella clamped her mouth shut.","Luna Margaret took a sip—and nearly scalded her tongue off. \"Ssss!\"","Nothing was going right today. She glared at her daughter. \"Isabella, are you trying to burn me alive?\"","\"I thought you’d let it cool first,\" Isabella muttered, pouting.","Luna Margaret set the cup aside, a bitter thought surfacing. If Eira were here, she’d never have been handed boiling water. Eira would’ve had her tucked in and cared for, everything just right.","What a mess they’d made.","Since she was awake and there was nothing seriously wrong, the doctor sent her home.","Isabella helped her mother into the car and climbed in beside her. Alpha Roger drove.","\"Mom, put your coat on.\"","A slip of paper fluttered out of the coat pocket.","\"What’s this?\" Isabella picked it up and handed it over.","Luna Margaret didn’t remember tucking anything into her pocket. Weary, she unfolded it.","[If you want your son’s money back from Serena, call this number.]","Eira’s handwriting.","Luna Margaret’s eyes flew wide. Isabella leaned in, curious, but her mother had already stuffed the note away.","A gleam flickered in Luna Margaret’s eyes. Of course she wanted her son’s money back.","Still, she didn’t fully trust Eira.","There were only two ways to claw that money back: settle it quietly, or sue. And a lawsuit would drag her son’s name through the mud of the pack. Absolutely not.","But letting Serena keep every cent? She couldn’t stomach that either.","--","On the drive back to Southridge Estates, Mrs. Jones asked, \"Miss Crawford, do you really think Sebastian’s mother will play along? He’s her own son.\"","Eira stared out the window. \"That money is her son’s too. And Margaret hates Serena.\"","\"Dealing with old hurt can be messy,\" Mrs. Jones said softly, sensing Eira’s thoughts. \"Like a blocked pipe. The dirt has to come out before things are clear.\"","\"Miss Crawford, tomorrow’s the weekend,\" Mrs. Jones said, changing the subject. \" Alpha Killian’s having his party. Miss Lila said she’d pick you up herself. You two can actually have some fun!\"","Right. The party. To the Sterlings, it was a celebration. To Eira, it was a chance for both project teams to meet early. That would make their work together smoother later on.","Mrs. Jones smiled. \"Miss Lila really likes you. She even thought about moving in to keep you company.\"","\"I won’t be living here long,\" Eira said.","Mrs. Jones started. \"What? You’re moving out?\"","Eira nodded.","\"Where would you go, Miss Crawford?\" Mrs. Jones thought. She needed to know. So she could tell Alpha Killian to buy a place there too. Be neighbors again.","Eira just said, \"We’ll see.\"","\"You’ll take me with you, won’t you?\" Mrs. Jones asked. \"I can’t be without you. Alpha Killian would kick me out of the pack.\"","Eira paused. \"I’ll take you.\"","\"Oh, thank Moon Goddess! Thank you, Miss Crawford!\" Mrs. Jones beamed. Crisis over. She almost lost her job as Alpha Killian’s love matchmaker.","Back at Southridge, Eira saw a huge pile of groceries by the door. \"Yours?\"","Mrs. Jones nodded. \"Starting today, you’re eating real meals. Three times a day, my way. We’re putting some meat on those bones.\"","Eira followed her into the kitchen and reached for a bag. Mrs. Jones swatted her hand away.","\"Miss Crawford! Don’t you go trying to do my job!\"","Eira didn’t believe her for a second. She grabbed another bag.","[What a good girl, ]Mrs. Jones thought, chuckling.","She walked behind Eira, gently pushing her hands away from things. The big, quiet house felt a little warmer.","That evening, Mrs. Jones cooked a huge meal. Then she hit her forehead. \"Old habit. Forgot to make less food. Miss Crawford, so nothing goes to waste, maybe we should find someone to help us eat it?\"","Her Alpha Killian, for example.","Eira nodded. \"Mrs. Jones, why don’t you send a plate over to Mr. Sterling?\""]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142 Alpha Victor’s Choice","paragraphs":["Mrs. Jones packed the meal into containers and carried it over to Number One of Southridge Estates.","Alpha Killian was already home from work.","\"Alpha Killian, your dinner,\" Mrs. Jones said. \"I did my best, Alpha. I cooked enough for two and dropped every hint I could that Miss Crawford should find someone to share it with. In the end, she only told me to bring it over to you.\"","That was so very Eira. Alpha Killian wasn’t surprised.","Mrs. Jones plated the food and set it on the table, delivering her report as she went. \"Alpha Killian, Miss Crawford’s planning to move soon. And she wants to claw back all the money her ex spent on his mistress over the years.\"","\"Move?\" Alpha Killian’s chopsticks paused mid-air. \"Move where?\"","\"She didn’t say. But don’t you worry, sir, Miss Crawford’s taking me with her. When the time comes, I’ll scout out whether the neighbors want to sell or rent.\"","Alpha Killian went quiet, thoughtful. \"Understood.\"","--","Alpha Victor was hosting Vincent Crawford at The Hawthorne.","Serena was there too, but her mind was elsewhere.","The reserved parking spot Eira had at Alpha Sebastian’s place. The custom walk-in closet. It all screamed: Eira’s not going anywhere.","Alpha Sebastian had never said it, but his actions were loud. He was pushing Serena out.","Alpha Victor caught his granddaughter drifting. He cut in with a low warning. \"Vincent’s almost here.\"","Serena snapped back to attention.","A server led Vincent Crawford in, sharp in a tailored suit. \"Alpha Victor, Serena, my apologies for running late. Had a few things to sort out.\"","He even brought a gift for Alpha Victor. \"A small token. I hope it’s to your liking.\"","\"Not at all, we arrived early.\" Alpha Victor’s face split into a warm smile. He cared more for the young man than any gift.","Alpha Sebastian, a married man, had only soured in his opinion. He never bothered with a proper visit.","\"Mr.Crawford ,\" Alpha Victor said, \"you’ve gone above and beyond this past week.\"","Vincent gave a humble shrug. \"You should call me by my name, same as Serena does. I only wish I’d actually been able to help.\"","Although Dr. Victor kept his honorary title, the Institute issued him a formal written censure and barred him from applying for or participating in grant-funded projects for three years.","At his age, the penalty hardly affected his career. He was already well past the usual age for retirement.","What mattered now was finding and training a successor.","\"I’m an old man. As long as the young ones are all right, that’s enough.\" Alpha Victor turned to his granddaughter. \"Serena, aren’t you going to raise a glass to Vincent?\"","Serena moved to lift her wine, but Vincent’s hand covered hers.","\"No need to stand on ceremony. Besides, you can’t hold your liquor.\"","Serena sat back down, a soft smile curving her lips. \"Thank you, Vincent.\"","He gave her a faint smile, then poured wine for himself and Alpha Victor.","The more Alpha Victor watched Vincent, the more he liked what he saw.","When Serena slipped away to the restroom, he seized the moment. \"You’re thirty this year, aren’t you?\"","Vincent nodded. \"Just turned thirty.\"","\"Not engaged? Not mated?\"","Vincent understood exactly where this was going. He gave a small laugh. \"I’m afraid not.\"","\"Is that by choice? Or is there someone you have your eye on?\" Alpha Victor knew the younger man had read him clearly. Now he was curious how Vincent would answer.","Vincent took a sip of his tea and spoke plainly. \"Alpha Victor, I do care for Serena.\"","Alpha Victor’s mood lifted instantly. \"That girl needs someone who can rein her in.\" Someone who could actually be of use to her, too.","Alpha Sebastian and Vincent were evenly matched in looks and capability—but the Hale Pack couldn’t hold a candle to the Crawfords.","\"She has someone she cares about,\" Vincent added.","\"You mean Sebastian?\" Alpha Victor waved it off. \"The girl’s been headstrong. I’ll set her straight. Alpha Sebastian has a mate. He and Serena will only ever be friends.\"","So Alpha Victor didn’t know Alpha Sebastian and Eira had dissolved their bond.","That worked in Vincent’s favor.","--","Serena returned and settled back into her seat, curious. \"Grandfather, what are you and Vincent plotting? You both look far too pleased with yourselves.\"","\"Your future, naturally.\" Alpha Victor looked at Vincent. \"I’m just an old set of bones. I’ll be counting on you to look after Serena from here on out.\"","Vincent’s gaze lingered on Serena, warm and deliberate. \"I will, Alpha Victor.\"","Serena’s eyes flickered.","\"There’s an old friend asking me to catch up tomorrow evening,\" Vincent said. \"Would you be free to join me, Serena?\"","Serena had been planning to catch Alpha Sebastian while he had the weekend free. She hadn’t seen him in days. She missed him fiercely. And she worried about him just as fiercely.","Alpha Victor answered before she could. \"She’s free.\"","Vincent turned to her. \"So, Serena? Care to join me?\"","Alpha Victor shot his granddaughter a look that clearly said, say yes, and quickly.","Serena nodded. \"I’m free.\"","Vincent smiled. \"I’ll pick you up at the Winthrop estate tomorrow afternoon.\"","\"All right.\"","She could see Alpha Sebastian in the morning, then spend the afternoon and evening with Vincent.","Getting closer to Vincent Crawford certainly couldn’t hurt. A little harmless flirting never killed anyone, right?"]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143 The Class","paragraphs":["Eira’s phone buzzed with Finn’s text first thing in the morning.","Beneath the polished apology, it was an invite to dinner.","Hale Group, one of his backers, had caused a stir at the last bidding event. Now he wanted to smooth things over.","Dinner? What for? Alpha Sebastian and Serena had already dug their own grave. Hale Group didn’t owe her an apology.","Besides, she had somewhere to be.","Eira texted back: I already have plans.","Finn stared at his phone, thoroughly deflated. He wanted to know what those plans were. More than that, he wanted to know where she was going.","So he started asking around.","Finn got rejected. Alpha Sebastian got the good news.","Eira had turned Finn down and was heading to her fertility class instead. Alpha Sebastian smiled when he saw the update.","Angry or not, she was still attending the classes he had signed her up for.","Too bad the Porsche wasn’t ready yet.","Otherwise, he would have driven over to pick her up and handed her the keys himself. He could still give them to her now and deal with the repairs later.","Alpha Sebastian dressed with unusual care before leaving. The champagne roses he had ordered arrived right on schedule.","He took the bouquet and headed downstairs.","The moment he stepped into the lobby, he ran straight into Serena.","\"Sebastian? Where are you off to?\" Serena’s eyes dropped to the roses. Her grip on her purse tightened.","He was caught off guard. \"What are you doing here?\"","\"We haven’t seen each other in days.\" She didn’t bother hiding it. \"I missed you. So I came.\"","His first reaction wasn’t happiness. It was a frown.\"Serena, I’ve got something to take care of today. I’ll come find you tomorrow.\"","He moved to step past her, but she caught his hand and cut straight to it. \"You’re going to see Eira, aren’t you?\"","He didn’t see the point in lying. He nodded.","\"Eira won’t even see you. I came to you, and you’d rather run off to her?\" Her eyes brimmed with wounded reproach.","Alpha Sebastian couldn’t quite meet her gaze. He looked away.","\"She’s my mate,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","That line again.","Serena couldn’t take it anymore. \"You’re mates in name only! You’ve never even touched her. What kind of mate is that?\"","Four years of never touching Eira had once made Alpha Sebastian feel like a devoted man. Now the thought brought nothing but regret—and a fresh sting of guilt.","\"Serena, whatever this is, it can wait.If I don’t go smooth things over with Eira, a summons from the court is going to land on both our doorsteps.\"","Serena froze.","In the heat of the moment, she’d forgotten all about that.","Eira wasn’t stupid. She’d known about them the very day it broke. She’d move on it, no question.","Serena’s hand fell away from his.","He was right to go. She couldn’t let a fit of jealousy cost her her reputation.","\"Where are you meeting her?\"","\"She has a class today.\"","\"What class? Did she finally get accepted for tenure? Which university is it?\" Serena’s face tightened, doubtful and irritated.","\"Fertility class,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Serena’s stomach dropped.","\"Fertility classes?\"","That was worse than tenure.","Alpha Sebastian wasn’t just supporting Eira’s career anymore.","He was planning for a future with her.","A family.","Pups.","Serena’s nails dug into her palm.","So where did that leave her?","She had spent so long believing Eira was temporary. That sooner or later, Alpha Sebastian would get tired of her and come back to the woman who actually belonged beside him.","But now?","Now Alpha Sebastian was thinking about children with Eira.","Before Serena could process the blow, Alpha Sebastian was already walking away, his pace brisk and his expression unreadable. He didn’t spare her another glance, as if their conversation had been nothing more than a few polite words exchanged with a stranger.","Her chest tightened.","Serena grabbed her purse and followed.","--","At the front desk, the receptionist recognized him instantly. \"Mr. Hale, here to pick up Mrs. Hale again?\"","\"Mm.\" He smiled. \"She’s about done, isn’t she?\"","\"Any minute now.\" The receptionist couldn’t stop gushing. \"Mrs. Hale never comes in late or leaves early. She’s so focused in class. Takes notes on everything.She’s clearly serious about starting a family.\"","The knot of anxiety that had been sitting in Alpha Sebastian’s chest for days finally began to loosen.","\"Thank you. She’s always been like that. Thorough about everything.\"","The receptionist smiled and headed toward the classroom, ready to let Mrs. Hale know her devoted husband was waiting for her again.","Rachel intercepted her in the hallway.","\"I’ve got it from here,\" Rachel said casually. \"You can head back to the desk.\"","\"Sure.\"","The receptionist turned and walked back.","Rachel waited until she was out of earshot, then pulled out her phone and called Eira.","\"Mr. Hale’s here again. Want me to keep him busy?\"","\"No need. Don’t bother covering for him.\"","\"He’ll ask what to do.\"","\"Just tell him the truth.\"","The call ended.","Rachel walked back to the front desk.","\"Mrs. Hale,\" the receptionist said with a smile.","Alpha Sebastian looked over.","He recognized Rachel immediately. She had been the one who handed him the pads the last time he came to pick Eira up.","His smile faded.\"Wait. What did you just call her?\"","\"Mrs. Hale?\"","Rachel gave him a polite look.\"I’m not Mrs. Hale. Nice to meet you, Mr. Hale.\"","The receptionist stared at her.\"But you’re the one who’s been taking the class.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.\"You’ve been taking the classes?\"","Rachel nodded.\"Every single one.\"","His eyes narrowed. \"Then where is Eira? When did she arrange for you to take her place?\"","\"From the beginning.\" Rachel shrugged. \"She didn’t want to attend, so she transferred her spot to me.\"","The receptionist looked horrified.","Alpha Sebastian said coldly.\"Then last time, she lied to me?\"","Rachel looked at the roses in his arms.\"If she didn’t want to take the class, why would she need someone to cover for her?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.\"Why would she do that?\"","Rachel gave him a flat look.\"Maybe because you cheated on her.\"","The receptionist’s eyes widened.She suddenly became very interested in anything that wasn’t happening in front of her.","\"You cheated on your wife and still expected her to prepare for a baby with you?\"Rachel shook her head.\"That’s pretty damn selfish, Mr. Hale.\"","Then she walked away.","Alpha Sebastian stood rooted to the spot.","Eira had never attended the fertility class.","Not once.","She had known about Serena long before the bidding disaster. She had never believed his \"we’re just friends\" excuse.","Instead, she had played along and let him think she was still preparing for the family he wanted.","She had been keeping the truth from him for more than a month.","Why?","And why had she gone to such lengths to deceive him?"]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144 The Landlord","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian caught up with Rachel and demanded she spell it out for him.","\"Mr. Hale,\" Rachel said, her voice dry. \"You were cheating on your wife while signing her up for fertility classes and planning a future with her. You wanted everything at once, and now you’re shocked that she chose not to play along.\"","\"So she decided not to have a baby with you and passed the classes on to someone else. That sounds pretty reasonable to me. Or should she have had a child just to give you another way to control her?\"","\"The reason she never told you is simple. She’s done with you. Whatever she felt is gone.\"","Alpha Sebastian burned with humiliation and rage.","Rachel didn’t give him the chance to open his mouth. \"Actually, I should be thanking you, Mr. Hale. Otherwise, I never could have afforded classes that cost tens of thousands. And honestly, I never could have said all that before now.\"","She looked positively enriched by the experience.Then Rachel turned on her heel and walked off.","Alpha Sebastian stood frozen where he was. Done with me?What was that supposed to mean?","Impossible. Eira had been so agreeable. No second-guessing, no suspicion. He hadn’t caught the slightest hint that anything was wrong.","He stood there clutching the roses, adrift, while the cold autumn wind lashed his face like a blade, cutting raw and deep.","He pulled out his phone and dialed Jordan. \"Find out if there are any listings for sale or lease at Southridge Estates. Get me the owner or the agent. I’m going in there today as a prospective buyer.\"","He was going to see Eira. If outsiders couldn’t get into Southridge Estates, he’d buy his way in.","Whatever it took, he was seeing Eira today.","If Eira could hide one thing from him, she could hide a second. If they didn’t sit down and have this out, this marriage really was heading for the end.","Alpha Sebastian sat in the car, his head pounding.","His phone lit up with message after message.","From Serena. She was informing him that Vincent had invited her to some friend’s gathering tonight.","[Go wherever the hell she wanted. What was the point of telling him?]","He killed the screen.","While he waited for Jordan’s update, every time Serena’s name popped up, he swiped it away without a glance.","He’d rather tap his fingers anxiously against the steering wheel than type her a single word back.","Not far away, Serena stared at the message that stubbornly refused to get a reply and slammed her palm against her own steering wheel, hard enough to send the horn blaring.","Alpha Sebastian never used to leave her on read. If he was slammed with work, he’d at least tell her he’d get back to her later.","This time she’d deliberately claimed she was heading out to a party with Vincent, and Alpha Sebastian had actually ignored it.","Not long ago, she’d hinted she might bring another man to a cocktail event, and Alpha Sebastian had snapped at her, telling her not to dare.","Alpha Sebastian didn’t care about her anymore. She refused to believe it.","Tonight she’d go out with Vincent, and she’d make damn sure to post a few photos online to needle him.","That particular nerve in a man needed constant prodding to keep the fear of losing alive.","--","Alpha Killian was standing in front of his closet, deciding between two ties, when Kate called.","\"Talk to me.\"","\"Alpha Sebastian wants to lease Number Eleven at Southridge Estates.\"","Kate usually handled requests like this without bothering Alpha Killian. This one was different.","The lease would be under Jordan’s name, Alpha Sebastian’s Beta and personal assistant. But the request had clearly come from Alpha Sebastian.","\"He wants to see the property today,\" Kate added. \"And he says it’s urgent.\"","Alpha Killian picked up the darker tie.","\"Let him come.\"","\"Yes, Alpha.\"","Alpha Killian ended the call, then switched to another line and called Lila.","\"What?\" His sister answered, sounding annoyed.","\"It’s time to take Eira out.\"","\"It’s four o’clock. The celebration dinner isn’t until six-thirty.\"","\"Stop arguing.\" Alpha Killian glanced at the luxury watches displayed behind the glass. \"I’ll fully equip your lab with the latest equipment.\"","Lila’s attitude changed instantly.","\"Seriously? You’re the best, Killian. We’ll head out right now.\"","Alpha Killian let out a quiet laugh as he fastened his watch.","\"Don’t spend the whole budget in one afternoon.\"","\"No promises.\"","The call ended.","Alpha Killian adjusted his tie and looked at his reflection.","Alpha Sebastian was coming for the estate because he wanted to meet Eira.","Alpha Killian had no intention of making that easy for him.","--","Alpha Sebastian and Jordan made it into Southridge Estates without trouble. They arrived in front of Number Eleven.","Alpha Sebastian instructed Jordan, \"Go park the car. And make yourself useful. See if you can spot anything.\"","Jordan caught the meaning at once. After parking, he began wandering casually around Southridge Estates, eyes sweeping every direction, trying to work out which villa Eira might be living in.","Alpha Sebastian stood at the door of Number Eleven. He stood. He waited. Half an hour. His calves ached.","The landlord was nowhere in sight.","For Eira. He could endure it.","Another ten minutes. Finally, figures approached.","It was Alpha Killian and Mrs. Jones.","Mrs. Jones, seeing Miss Crawford’s ex-husband, looked him up and down like he was a specimen under glass.","The scrutiny made Alpha Sebastian’s skin crawl.","What made it worse was that the property owner was Alpha Killian. Of all the damn Alphas.","Mrs. Jones stopped in front of him.","\"You’re here about Number Eleven?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"My employer is asking four million dollars a year,\" she said. \"There’s a three-year minimum, and the rent must be paid annually in advance.\"","Alpha Sebastian barely opened his mouth before Alpha Killian cut in.","\"You sure you can afford it? Maybe collect what Ms. Winthrop owes you first. Then you can figure out if you’ve got enough left to pay the rent.\""]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145 Bait","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian had already swallowed a full helping of humiliation that morning. Now Alpha Killian was serving him a second course. The words stuck in his throat like a stone.","\"A billion-dollar empire behind you, and you’re renting out your property?\" Alpha Sebastian’s mouth twisted.","Alpha Killian renting meant he was bleeding money somewhere. That kind of news could shake the market.","Alpha Killian didn’t even blink. \"I’ve got too many houses and no mistress to gift them to. Empty is empty.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave him a look full of anger. Just helpless anger.","Alpha Killian raised a brow. His voice was challenging. \"So, Alpha Sebastian. Still renting, or not?\"","Alpha Sebastian came here only for Eira. He would sign the lease if Jordan found her.","\"If you’re going to rent the place, Alpha Killian, aren’t you going to open the door and let your tenant look?\" Alpha Sebastian tried to buy time.","Alpha Killian gave Mrs. Jones a quick look.","She stepped forward and unlocked the door.","Alpha Sebastian walked inside. Alpha Killian and Mrs. Jones stayed in the courtyard.","\"Alpha,\" Mrs. Jones whispered. \"I’ve hung Miss Crawford’s old clothes out at Number Twenty.\"","Number Twenty was the other empty villa Alpha Killian owned.","--","When Jordan came around the corner, he stopped.","He saw Alpha Killian standing in the courtyard. [Wasn’t Alpha Killian supposed to have a celebration dinner today?]","\"Alpha Killian.\" Jordan nodded.","Alpha Sebastian’s voice barked from inside. \"Get in here.\"","Jordan hurried inside to report. \"Alpha. Luna Eira is living here at Southridge Estates. It’s Number Twenty. Not next door.\"","\"You’re sure?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","Jordan spoke with confidence. \"Positive, Alpha. Her clothes are still drying. The place is clean.\"","Alpha Killian and Mrs. Jones walked in just then.","\"Well, sir?\" Mrs. Jones asked. \"Are you taking the place or not?\"","Alpha Sebastian thought for a second. He’d take it. Four million a year. He could find the money.","It would leave him almost broke, but he had to spend money to catch her.","He wouldn’t let Alpha Killian see him hesitate. He signed the contract fast. Wrote the check right there.","Off to the side, Jordan’s eye twitched.","[ Alpha Sebastian, you’re almost out of money. You don’t have this kind of cash. The company is losing money fast]","\"Signing so eagerly, Alpha Sebastian.\" Alpha Killian’s voice was smooth. \"All for Eira?\"","That one line was enough. Alpha Sebastian tore the check loose and pushed it forward.","Mrs. Jones took it after Alpha Killian nodded.","Money in hand, they left.","Jordan felt something was wrong. A rental? And Alpha Killian came himself? It didn’t make sense.","Alpha Sebastian turned to him. \"Is anyone at Number Twenty right now?\"","Jordan shook his head. \"No.\"","\"She’s probably at the Silix Institute.\" Alpha Sebastian sighed. \"We’ll wait. Later.\"","They both sat down.","--","Money in hand, Alpha Killian and Mrs. Jones headed off toward Number Nine.","\"What do we do with the money?\" Mrs. Jones asked.","\"You take it. Use it for Eira’s groceries,\" Killian said. \"Four million a year. Enough?\"","Mrs. Jones’s mind was already racing. \"That should cover it, Alpha.\"","\"Good.\" Killian still thought it was too little.","He handed her a card. \"If it’s not enough, use this. And get Eira to move out sooner.\"","Mrs. Jones nodded. \"Don’t you worry, Alpha. I’ll have Miss Crawford all packed up by the weekend and a car on standby.\"","\"Drive it straight over where?\"","Mrs. Jones shook her head. \"Not yet.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing, but the look on his face said enough.","Mrs. Jones sighed. \"Oh, don’t look at me like that. I’m working on it.\"","She paused.","\"Although, if you’re worried about Miss Crawford, you might want to head to the yacht.\"","Alpha Killian finally looked at her.","\"Why?\"","\"Because she’ll be surrounded by people. And you’re hardly the only Alpha who’ll notice her.\" Mrs. Jones gave him a pointed look. \"Wait too long, and someone else might get there first.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"Get the car ready.\"","--","Isabella was sprawled on the couch, scrolling through Serena’s latest post.","A luxury yacht. A deck full of handsome, well-dressed men. The kind of life Isabella had always dreamed about.","She sat up at once and opened Serena’s chat.","[Where are you? Is this some kind of party?]","Serena took a moment to reply. She knew Isabella too well to miss what she wanted.","[Want to come?]","Isabella’s fingers flew over the screen.","[Would that be okay?]","The answer came back almost immediately.","[Absolutely.]","Isabella jumped off the couch and rushed to her room. She needed a new dress, perfect hair, and a full makeover. If she caught the eye of one of those men, her life could change overnight.","And Serena would help her.","Isabella spent nearly an hour getting ready before finally walking out in a light summer dress.","Luna Margaret was still on the sofa, staring at her phone. Ever since she had come home from the hospital, she had worn the same angry expression.","\"Mom, I’m heading out.\"","Luna Margaret looked up and frowned. \"Out again? You’ll freeze in that dress.\"","\"I’ll bring a coat. It’s warm on the yacht.\"","\"A yacht?\" Luna Margaret’s eyes narrowed. \"Who’s taking you?\"","\"Serena, obviously.\"","Luna Margaret’s face darkened. She lifted a hand.","\"Sit down. You’re not going.\"","Isabella stared at her. \"What? Why not?\"","\"From now on, you stay away from Serena. That’s not up for debate.\" Luna Margaret’s voice was sharp. \"She isn’t the person you think she is.\"","Isabella’s brows drew together.","\"Mom, what are you talking about? You loved Serena. You wanted her to marry my brother. She’s always been good to us. She’s bought us beautiful gifts and taken us to the best places.\"","\"Those gifts were paid for with your brother’s money!\"","Luna Margaret’s anger finally boiled over.","\"Every dollar Serena spent on this family came from Sebastian’s accounts. She wasn’t being generous. She was spending your brother’s money and making all of us thank her for it.\""]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146 The Grapevine","paragraphs":["\"Mom, that’s insane.\" Isabella shook her head. \"Serena has always been good to me. She’s bought me dresses, handbags, and shoes. Whenever Sebastian and I argued, she took my side.\"","To Isabella, Serena had everything the Hales valued. A respected family name, beauty, charm, and confidence.","\"She doesn’t have to be a genius to be loved,\" Isabella added. \"Not everyone can be Eira.\"","Luna Margaret’s temper finally snapped.","\"You’ve been letting Serena play you for years.\" She slapped her hand against the arm of the sofa. \"Your brother lost that bid because investigators found a paper trail between him and Serena. Huge payments. They suspect he bribed her.\"","Isabella’s face paled, but she still refused to believe it.","\"Where did you hear that? Did Eira tell you? Maybe she’s trying to turn us against Serena.\"","\"The evidence came from Sebastian’s financial records,\" Luna Margaret said. \"Do you think I nearly passed out for no reason?\"","Isabella fell silent.","\"Your brother sent Serena three hundred thousand dollars every month,\" Luna Margaret continued. \"Every meal, hotel room, designer outfit, and luxury car was paid for with his money. While she lived like royalty, Sebastian kept the rest of us on a budget.\"","\"She didn’t force him to give it to her,\" Isabella muttered.","\"No, she just knew exactly how to get him to open his wallet.\" Luna Margaret pointed at her. \"You are not going anywhere with Serena tonight. If you keep seeing her, I’ll drag you home myself.\"","Isabella stared at her mother. Luna Margaret was completely serious.","\"But that can’t be true.\"","\"Look at Eira,\" Luna Margaret said. \"She never lived better than us or wasted Sebastian’s money on herself. She used her own salary to cover the household expenses. Serena, on the other hand, took everything she could get.\"","Her gaze fell on the designer handbag hanging from Isabella’s arm.","\"All those gifts bought your loyalty. You thought Serena was generous, but she was spending Sebastian’s money and making you feel grateful for it.\"","Isabella slowly lowered her arm.","For the first time, the handbag no longer felt like a gift.","Luna Margaret looked away, her anger replaced by bitter regret.","She had wanted Serena as her daughter-in-law. She had defended her and blamed Eira whenever Alpha Sebastian was unhappy.","Now she understood the difference.","Eira had worked, managed the household, cared for Isabella, supported Alpha Sebastian, and handled the pack’s daily affairs. Serena had offered expensive gifts, while Eira had done the actual work.","No wonder Roger had been afraid to tell Alpha Sebastian about the divorce. No wonder he had asked Luna Margaret to keep quiet while he searched for a way to undo it.","But the divorce was final.","Eira was gone, and the family had driven away the woman who had held everything together.","Luna Margaret made up her mind. She was going to get Alpha Sebastian’s money back, even if it meant swallowing her pride and asking Eira for help.","\"That woman fooled this entire family, especially your brother. He handed her everything he had. How could he be so stupid?\"","\"Mom, is all of this really true?\" Isabella asked.She already believed most of it. Anger burned in her eyes as her hand curled into a fist.","\"I’m going to find Serena and make her tell me the truth. If she really took my brother’s money, she and I are done.\"","Luna Margaret didn’t stop her.","Instead, she picked up the note Eira had left behind and dialed the number on it.","Eira glanced at the unfamiliar number.\"Hello?\"","\"Eira. This is Margaret Hale.\"","Eira leaned back in her chair. So she’d finally figured out what Serena had been doing.","\"What can I do for you?\"","Luna Margaret hesitated. Her pride clearly hated what she was about to say. \"I think we need to talk. About the money Serena took from Sebastian.\"","Eira almost laughed.","\"I’m busy tonight,\" Eira said. \"Call me tomorrow. We can talk in person.\"","\"Fine. But don’t make me wait.\"","Eira smiled faintly at the impatience in Luna Margaret’s voice and ended the call.","Lila was leaning against the yacht’s railing nearby.","\"Who was that?\"","\"Sebastian’s mother.\"","\"What does she want? Don’t tell me she’s calling to pick another fight.\"Lila asked. Mrs. Jones had complained about Luna Margaret often enough that the description came naturally.","\"She wants to make a deal.\" Eira looked out over the dark water as the wind moved across the deck. \"She wants to help recover the money Serena took from Sebastian.\"","Lila’s eyes lit up. \"Now that’s interesting. With Luna Margaret on your side, this just got a lot easier. Did Susan give you a list of the evidence she needs?\"","\"She did. Bank records, transfer details, messages, photos, and anything else that connects Sebastian to Serena.\"","\"Susan is good,\" Lila said with a grin. \"Even if Serena hires Vincent, she’s still going to have a serious fight on her hands. Financial recovery isn’t his area.\"","Before Eira could answer, someone appeared on the deck below them.","Lila leaned over the railing.","\"Is that Vincent?\"","Eira looked down.","Vincent had taken off his black coat and placed it around Serena’s shoulders. Serena stood beside him in a thin dress, looking cold and miserable. From above, she appeared to be leaning against his chest.","Lila’s mouth curved with amusement.\"Well, that’s convenient. Does Vincent know he’s comforting another man’s mistress?\"","\"He probably doesn’t know the whole story,\" Eira said.","She pulled out her phone and took one picture.","Lila stared at her. \"Why are you taking photos?\"","\"To give Sebastian something else to worry about.\" Eira sent the picture. \"Maybe it will keep him busy and stop him from calling me.\"","Her phone had been flooded with calls and messages from unknown numbers lately. Alpha Sebastian never said anything openly threatening. He only kept asking to see her, always polite and careful.","That made him harder to shut down.","Lila glanced at Eira’s phone. \"Why not block him?\"","\"He keeps using different numbers.\"","\"Block them. Turn on call screening. Or just change your number.\""]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147 Caught in the Crossfire","paragraphs":["Eira pulled her gaze from the water.","\"I can’t change that number,\" she said quietly. \"Two years ago, I met a thirteen-year-old pup at the Omega orphanage. A distant relative took him in, but only because they wanted free labor. I gave him that number in case he ever needed me. If I shut it down, he might have no way to reach me.\"","Lila’s expression softened, but only for a moment.","\"Of course you did.\" She glanced toward the water and shivered. \"Sebastian is such a pain. It’s freezing out here. Let’s go back inside.\"","\"Sure.\"","They turned toward the door.","On the deck below, Serena happened to glance up. \"Eira?\"","Vincent followed her gaze, but the upper deck was already empty.","\"I could have sworn I saw Eira,\" Serena said. \"And Lila was with her.\"","She remembered hearing that the entire third floor had been reserved for a private party.\"Do you know who booked the third floor?\"","Vincent shook his head. \"No. Logan and the others should be inside. We can ask them.\"","They walked into the private lounge, where Vincent’s old friend Logan Harris was waiting with two guests, a man and a woman.","Serena did not recognize the woman.","The man was another story.","Barry Wood.","Serena’s smile turned brittle.","\"Vincent, it’s been a while,\" Logan said.","\"Only a few months.\" Vincent pulled him into a quick hug.","Logan turned to his guests. \"This is Barry Wood. I’ve known him my whole life. He’s a doctor, a pain in the ass, and somehow still one of my best friends.\"","Barry nudged him with an elbow. \"Keep talking. I’m enjoying this.\"","\"And this is Fiona Carter,\" Logan continued. \"She’s a friend too.\"","He gestured toward Vincent. \"The famous attorney Vincent Crawford. Our families go way back. We’re distant cousins, if you go far enough up the family tree, but the older generation can argue over the details.\"","His eyes slid to Serena, brows waggling. \"And this is? Come on, Counselor, don’t be rude.\"","Vincent stood beside Serena. \"Serena Winthrop. A friend I met while traveling overseas.\"","Logan raised an eyebrow. The coat made Serena look like far more than a casual acquaintance.","Fiona noticed it too.","Logan glanced between them. \"You two know each other?\"","Fiona looked Serena up and down. \"Not personally. But I’ve heard the name.\"","Barry leaned lazily on one hand. \"Oh, I definitely know Miss Winthrop.\"","Logan blinked. \"Everybody knows her but me? What, I skip town for a while and miss the whole show?\"","Fiona smiled faintly. \"She’s Sebastian Hale’s... friend.\"","\"Wow. Subtle,\" Barry said dryly.","The tension in the room grew impossible to miss.","Logan cleared his throat. \"Whatever the story is, tonight is a clean slate.\"","Fiona and Barry exchanged a glance before giving Serena polite but distant nods.","Serena understood the message. She was not welcome.","Everyone took a seat.","Serena sat beside Vincent, stiff and uncomfortable. She wanted to leave, but she did not want to embarrass him.To break the silence, Vincent asked, \"So, who booked the third floor?\"","\"Sterling,\" Logan said. \"It’s a company retreat.\"","\"More like a victory party,\" Fiona said. \"Hale Group got crushed in the bid, and Sterling walked away with the contract.\"","Barry gave her a look. \"Come on. Losing to Killian Sterling isn’t exactly embarrassing.\"","\"He only won because he played dirty,\" Fiona muttered.","\"You still need something to hide before anyone can use it against you,\" Barry said. \"No secrets, no leverage.\"","Fiona had no answer. Her eyes shifted to Serena.","Serena kept a polite smile on her face, but her jaw was tight.","Vincent noticed. He immediately regretted bringing her.","\"Logan just got back in town,\" he said. \"Maybe we can leave business out of dinner.\"","The warning in his voice was quiet but clear.","Fiona and Barry were not intimidated by him, but they knew when to stop. They raised their glasses.","For a moment, it seemed the subject was over.","Then Logan looked Serena over. \"With that kind of poise, I would have guessed you were a dancer.\"","Barry nearly choked on his drink.","\"Seriously, Logan?\" Fiona said.","\"What? I was making conversation.\"","\"Serena is a research scientist,\" Barry said.","\"Was,\" Fiona corrected.","Logan blinked. \"Wait. What happened?\"","\"Logan,\" Vincent cut in, \"this isn’t helping. Serena and I are going to call it a night.\"","He couldn’t stand watching her sit there and take the insults.","Serena lifted her chin and gave him a soft smile, as if she was fine. Her eyes, however, were bright with hurt.","Fiona let out a short laugh.","Logan’s expression cooled. \"Could you two cut me some slack?\"","\"I’ve given you plenty.\" Fiona’s smile disappeared. \"We’ve known each other for years, so I’m going to be blunt. Hale Group, one of Carter Group’s portfolio investments, just lost the contract. Serena’s name came up in the investigation, and so did Sebastian Hale’s.\"","Logan’s face changed.","\"She’s involved with a mated Alpha,\" Fiona continued. \"Sebastian has a mate, and you still brought Serena here and wrapped your coat around her like some lovesick teenager.\"","Vincent’s expression hardened. \"Watch yourself.\"","\"I’m not insulting you. I’m trying to understand you.\" Fiona looked at him in disbelief. \"You’re a Crawford, Vincent. You should know better than to get dragged into someone else’s scandal.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around her glass.","Fiona turned to her.\"And you’re quite the actress. You sit there with those wounded eyes and pretend this is all innocent. My father used his influence to keep the story from becoming public. Don’t mistake that for innocence.\"","Serena’s face went pale.","Fiona pushed back her chair. \"Logan, you and the counselor can catch up. I’m leaving.\"","She walked out.","Logan opened his mouth, but nothing came out.","\"I’ll go after her,\" Barry said.","Logan waved him off. \"Yeah, go.\"","Barry slipped out after Fiona.","For the first time that evening, Serena turned to Vincent. \"I’m sorry. This happened because of me.\"","\"It’s not your fault,\" Vincent said. \"Sebastian made you believe his relationship with Eira was over in everything but name. They don’t know what he told you.\"","Logan stayed quiet.","[Buddy, I think you’re the one being played.]","\"It’s fine,\" he said at last. \"Let’s just finish dinner. I only wanted to catch up with Vincent. I thought bringing everyone together would make the night more fun.\"","He glanced toward the door.\"I didn’t expect it to turn into this.\"","Barry and Fiona had disagreed about almost everything for years. Tonight was the first time they had ended up on the same side.","Somehow, Serena had managed to unite them.","Logan looked at Vincent.","[Open your eyes, man.]"]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148 The Wolf and the Doctor","paragraphs":["Fiona and Barry stepped out onto the main deck, the cool night air hitting them.","Fiona stopped. \"Are you heading back?\"","\"I’m going up,\" Barry said. Alpha Killian had invited him to the victory party on the upper deck tonight. But with Logan freshly back in town, Barry had skipped the celebration earlier.","\"Fine. I’ll go home alone,\" Fiona said.","Barry tried his luck. \"How about you come up with me for a bit? Just for a drink. Then I’ll make sure you get home safe.\"","\"Do you want me dead? Just say so.\" Fiona shot him a look. \"Carter Group and Sterling Pack are rivals. If I show up at a Sterling party, everyone’s going to think Carter’s waving the white flag. No wonder you’re Alpha Killian’s personal doctor. You’ve got no shame.\"","Barry just stood there. So much for good intentions.","He turned toward the stairs.","Just then, Eira was coming down from the upper deck. She’d stepped outside earlier to take a call, but Alpha Killian had startled her. Her phone had slipped and tumbled down to the level below.","Barry nearly ran into Eira on the landing.","\"Eira?\"","\"Dr. Wood.\"","At the name, Fiona’s head snapped around. [Wasn’t this Alpha Sebastian’s mate? ]","\"Where are you off to, Eira?\"","\"Retrieving my phone.\"","Before Barry could ask another question, Alpha Killian’s tall frame appeared at the top of the stairs, long legs carrying him down at an unhurried pace. His cold gaze slid sideways, landing on Barry.","\"Weren’t you having dinner with Logan?\"","\"Logan and Vincent had things to discuss, so I ducked out early.\" Barry stepped aside to let Eira pass. He fell into step behind Alpha Killian, like a loyal shadow. \"I’ll head back upstairs, Alpha. Take your time.\"","Fiona’s eyes moved between the three of them. A woman’s instinct was rarely wrong. Hers was screaming that Alpha Killian’s interest in Alpha Sebastian’s mate was anything but innocent.","She wanted to see for herself what made Eira so special that both Alpha Sebastian and Alpha Killian had taken an interest in her.","Suddenly, Fiona caught his arm. \"Hey, weren’t you just offering to walk me up?\"","Barry looked at her. \"Don’t start trouble, Fiona. If you make a scene, the Carters will back you up. If I do, no one’s got my back, and my grandmother’s too old to survive the shock.\"","\"Relax.\" She waved him toward the stairs.","Barry did not relax. But there was no arguing with a Carter, so up they went.","--","Eira had just bent to pick up her phone from the second level deck, where it had fallen, when a hand beat her to it.","The device settled into Alpha Killian’s warm palm. \"I’ll get you a new one.\"","\"The one still works,\" Eira said, reaching for it. Their fingers brushed.","Alpha Killian felt a bloom of cold.","He studied her. Turtleneck, thick trousers, a cashmere coat. Her lips were pink, not blue. Yet her fingertips were ice.","\"Why are your hands so cold?\"","Eira was busy texting Miss Gwen back, having accidentally dropped the earlier call. The soft concern from above made her look up.","\"Are you cold?\" Alpha Killian asked again.","Eira wiggled her slender, pale fingers. \"It’s normal. Most women run cold. Winter always turns our hands and feet to ice.\"","She finished the message. \"Let’s head back, Mr. Sterling.\"","Alpha Killian nodded. \"Who was calling?\"","Eira sighed. The legendary man of few words was a myth. \"Home.\"","His eyes flickered. \"The orphanage?\"","\"Miss Gwen sent me the height and weight chart for the kids.\" A faint smile touched her mouth. \"I can order the winter coats now.\"","Alpha Killian’s brow lifted, and the ghost of a smile pulled at his lips.","The pleasant moment didn’t last. Along both banks the city blazed with light, skyscrapers running their signature light shows. A river cruiser drifted past, sending ripples fanning across the water.","On their deck, a new group emerged from the lounge, stepping into the evening air.","Two groups came face to face.","The moment Logan spotted Alpha Killian, he moved in fast. \"Alpha Killian.\"","\"Logan.\"","Logan never could look at Alpha Killian without a pang. They were roughly the same age, yet Alpha Killian had taken the Alpha role at twenty while Logan, pushing thirty, still had a father who refused to step aside. Comparison really was the thief of joy.","Then Logan’s gaze shifted to Eira.","The moment he got a good look at her face, he stiffened.[Why does she look so familiar?]","With the disaster of Vincent, Serena, and Lainey fresh in mind, he decided not to guess.","Instead he asked politely, \"And this is?\"","Alpha Killian answered. \"A business partner.\"","Eira gave a calm nod.","Logan’s whole demeanor changed. A Sterling business partner was no ordinary person. He extended a hand. \"What should I call you?\"","Eira started to reach out.","Then Logan caught the warning frost in Alpha Killian’s eyes and yanked his hand back.","Eira’s hand hung in the empty air. Awkward.","This time the look Alpha Killian aimed at him carried more than warning. It carried murder.","\"Just call me Eira.\" Unbothered, she withdrew her hand, and her eyes collided with Serena’s, then with Vincent’s beside her.","Both of them had been staring at her.","Logan pressed on. \"What line of work are you in, Ms. Eira?\"","\"She’s in research,\" Alpha Killian said.","Logan turned to him. Was that pride on the man’s face?","\"You’re in research too? So is a friend of Vincent’s. I wonder if you two know each other.\"","Right in the sore spot.","Serena was speechless. Vincent couldn’t fathom what had gotten into Logan tonight.","Eira nodded. \"We do.\"","Alpha Killian added, \"Serena was Eira’s former subordinate, more or less.\"","If Logan couldn’t read the room now, he deserved to be called a fool.He wisely shut his mouth.","Vincent moved to leave with Serena. She’d taken enough hits tonight, thanks to him. He was getting her home, no matter what.","As it happened, the cruiser was pulling in at the next dock for a brief stop.","The boat had barely settled when Alpha Sebastian appeared in full view of everyone.","Serena spotted him first, her face lighting up. From his frantic expression, she assumed he’d seen her post and come running, jealous.","In truth, the first person Alpha Sebastian looked for was Eira.","The moment he’d received a text from Jordan about Alpha Killian hosting a victory party on this very yacht, his gut had told him Eira might be here.","Fortune had smiled on him. Eira was here."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149 The Fall","paragraphs":["Serena’s nails dug into her palms.","[This was impossible. Alpha Sebastian had come for her, not Eira.]","The moment he stepped onto the deck, she hurried toward him with a bright smile.","\"Sebastian.\"","Only then did he seem to notice her. He looked honestly surprised, as if he had walked right past her without seeing her.","Serena’s smile faltered.","Eira had already turned away, ready to leave the scene, when Alpha Sebastian’s voice cut through the night.","\"Eira!\"","He walked straight past Serena as though she were part of the furniture.","The hurt on her face lasted only a second, but Vincent saw it. His chest tightened.","He almost told her the truth. Eira and Alpha Sebastian were already divorced. Maybe if Serena knew, she would stop putting herself through this.","But before he could say anything, Alpha Killian stepped in front of Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Killian moved with calm precision, placing his broad frame between the two of them and drawing Eira behind him.","\"Watch yourself, Alpha Sebastian.\" Alpha Killian’s voice was low. His eyes held a cold warning.","TThis was Sterling Group’s victory celebration. The deck was filled with Sterling employees and members of Eira’s research team.","Alpha Sebastian had no business causing a scene in front of them. An Alpha didn’t air his dirty laundry in front of his pack.","He certainly didn’t do it in front of a rival pack’s celebration.","Everyone understood that a leader had to protect his reputation. You did not drag your private mess into public and expect to walk away clean.","Especially when you were the one who’d been caught cheating.","Alpha Sebastian stopped a few feet away.","\"Eira.\" His voice softened. \"There’s a lot I need to explain. When you’re finished here, let me take you home. Please.\"","\"No.\"","Her answer was quiet, but it left no room for discussion.","Alpha Sebastian froze.","\"There are things I can explain if you’ll just give me a chance.\"","\"What’s left to explain?\" Eira looked at his face, and disgust twisted in her stomach. \"You love Serena. Then go be with her. I’m not stopping you.\"","\"Eira!\"","His pupils widened. The edges of his eyes turned red.","She was his mate. How could she dismiss him so easily?","Serena watched his reaction, and it felt like a knife twisting between her ribs.","Alpha Sebastian was fighting back tears.","For Eira.","\"Vincent,\" she whispered. \"Do you think he still has feelings for her?\"","Vincent’s jaw tightened.","He had no answer that would not hurt her.","Nearby, Logan watched the scene unfold. At this point, he would have had to be blind to miss what was going on.","The pieces finally fell into place.","The woman Alpha Sebastian had married was Eira. Serena was the other woman. And Eira had once been Serena’s boss.","[I am way out of my depth here.]","Logan pulled out his phone and texted Barry and Fiona.","[Where are you two?]","A few minutes later, Barry and Fiona stepped onto the upper deck and looked down.","The scene below had gone completely sideways. Alpha Killian stood between Eira and Alpha Sebastian, while Serena and Vincent remained nearby. It looked less like a party and more like two packs preparing for a territorial fight.","\"Alpha Killian, Eira,\" Barry called. \"There you are. We’ve been looking everywhere.\"","Alpha Killian glanced up, then shifted his eyes toward Eira and the stairs.","Upstairs.","Eira caught the message at once and headed upstairs without hesitation.","Alpha Sebastian tried to follow, but Sterling security blocked his way.","The entire third deck had been reserved for the party, and they had no intention of letting him through.","He could have left.","Instead, he stayed by the railing. If he waited until the boat docked, he might still get a chance to speak with Eira.","Too many questions were tormenting him.","Why had she refused the house? Why had she skipped the fertility classes? Why had she lied to him?","And why had she looked at him like a stranger when they were mates?","\"Sebastian, you’re really going to wait here for her?\" Serena asked, stepping closer. \"You only want to explain the money and the investments, right? It’s freezing out here. Come inside with me.\"","She was already using the explanation they had agreed on. The money Alpha Sebastian had given her was supposed to be treated as loans and investments, not support for an affair.","Alpha Sebastian shook his head.","\"I’m staying right here.\" He glanced at Serena. \"It’s cold. Go back with Vincent.\"","Serena stared at him.","He was sending her away with another man, and he did not look jealous at all.","Before she could respond, Vincent came over.","\"Serena, the boat is docking soon. We should get ready to leave.\"","With so many people watching, Serena forced a smile.\"Sure.\"","She turned toward the railing.","For one brief second, she looked back at Alpha Sebastian.","Then she went over the side.","\"Serena!\"","Her body hit the water with a loud splash.","\"Man overboard!\" Logan shouted.","Serena surfaced a few yards from the boat, thrashing in the freezing river.","\"Help!\" she cried. \"Sebastian, help me!\"","Vincent rushed toward the railing, but Logan caught him around the waist.","\"Don’t even think about it. That water is ice-cold.\"","\"She can’t swim!\"","\"She jumped, Vincent. I saw her do it.\"","Alpha Sebastian heard the shouting and ran to the railing. The moment he saw Serena struggling below, he jumped in without hesitation.","The cold water hit him like a punch. He surfaced, fought through the current, and reached Serena within seconds.","\"Get the crew!\" Vincent shouted.","The cruiser had already begun pulling away from the dock, so the crew turned it around. By the time they reached Serena, Alpha Sebastian was barely keeping himself above water.","The crew hauled them both back onboard.","Serena coughed up river water and collapsed against Alpha Sebastian. A moment later, she passed out.","Vincent watched in silence, his expression hard to read.","Did she really have to risk her life just to see whether Alpha Sebastian would come after her?","\"Get her home,\" Vincent said at last.","Alpha Sebastian lifted Serena into his arms and carried her off the boat.","He had promised to wait for Eira.","In the end, he left with Serena instead.","The people on deck turned toward Eira. Sympathy showed in their faces.","Eira did not react. She simply raised her phone and took several pictures. Then she started recording.","The entire rescue was now on file."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150 A Loan, Not a Gift","paragraphs":["Vincent did not get into Alpha Sebastian’s car. He was still shaken by what he had just witnessed. The drop from the deck to the river was at least twenty feet, and the water was cold enough to cause serious harm.","The woman he thought he knew did not match the woman who had just jumped into freezing water over a man.","Logan glanced at him and sighed. \"Let me drive you back to the hotel.\"","He paused before adding, \"And stop worrying about Serena. Alpha Sebastian jumped in after her. He’s not going to leave her stranded.\"","Logan still couldn’t understand why Vincent kept getting pulled deeper into Serena’s problems. She was not the only woman in the world. A man like Vincent, the Crawford heir and one of the most successful attorneys in the country, could date anyone he wanted. Yet he was risking his reputation for her.","\"Why are you getting involved in this?\" Logan asked. \"Alpha Killian is involved now, and your mom has close ties to the Reed Pack. This whole situation is a minefield.\"","\"Did Serena pull you out of a burning building or something, man?\"","Vincent stared out the window. \"It’s complicated.\"","Logan waited, but Vincent said nothing more.","Logan understood that much. He decided not to press.","For a moment, he considered mentioning how familiar Eira’s face had seemed. Then he changed his mind. Saying it in front of Vincent could sound like he was accusing Vincent’s father of having an affair.","That was not his problem.","So Logan kept his mouth shut.","--","Across town, Serena sat propped against the headboard, pale and wrapped in a blanket as she watched Alpha Sebastian move around the room.","On the way back from the docks, he’d stopped at a 24-hour pharmacy for cold medicine and a thermometer. Now he was in the kitchen, stirring the medicine into some warm broth and fussing over her like he used to when she was the woman he loved most.","For a moment, it felt like old times. Like it was just the two of them in the whole world.","The thermometer beeped. Alpha Sebastian picked it up and checked the reading.","\"No fever. Take the medicine anyway, just to be safe.\"","\"Thanks.\" Serena took a sip from the mug.","He waited until she finished before getting to the point.","\"Why did you jump?\"","Serena blinked. \"What?\"","\"Why did you jump into the river?\"","\"I slipped.\" She matched his flat tone. \"It was an accident.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not believe her for a second.","\"You know I can’t swim. Why would I...\"","\"Exactly. You can’t swim.\" His voice hardened. \"That’s the problem.\"","She gave him a soft smile. \"You were worried about me.\"","Alpha Sebastian opened his mouth, then closed it again. After a moment, he let out a slow breath.","\"Don’t ever do that again, Serena. Whatever is going on between us...\"","There were things he needed to say, but she looked too pale and exhausted. Tonight was not the time.","\"Get some rest.\" He stood.","\"Where are you going?\"","\"Home.\"","He glanced down at his soaked jeans. The wet fabric clung coldly to his legs.","Serena wanted to ask him to stay, but she held back. If someone took a picture of him leaving her apartment in the morning, the scandal would be impossible to explain.","\"Will you come by tomorrow?\" she asked, followed by a soft cough.","Alpha Sebastian looked away.","\"Maybe. If you can’t take care of yourself, call the Winthrop family’s housekeeper.\"","Then he left.","Alpha Sebastian kept a spare change of clothes in his car. After changing, he drove straight back to the pier.","The cruiser had just docked. Sterling employees were filing off in a steady stream, which meant the celebration was over.","Alpha Sebastian scanned the crowd.","Eira was nowhere to be seen.","Then he spotted Isabella near the entrance, craning her neck as she searched the disembarking passengers.","He got out of the car.","The moment Isabella saw him, she hurried over.","\"Sebastian? What are you doing here?\"","\"I could ask you the same thing.\"","\"I came to find Serena.\" Their mother had told her everything that evening, and Isabella needed to know whether it was true.","She had been waiting at the pier for what felt like forever. Because of the man-overboard emergency, the cruiser had returned to a different slip than expected. By the time Isabella finally boarded, Serena was gone and would not answer her phone.","She was cold, furious, and in no mood to leave without answers.","If she could not confront Serena, she would question her brother instead.","\"Mom told me about the money,\" Isabella said. \"All those years, you were spending it on Serena, weren’t you? Eira wasn’t the one wasting it. Tell me the truth.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s pupils narrowed.","Sterling employees were still walking past them, and Isabella was speaking loudly enough for half the pier to hear.","\"No,\" he said flatly.","Isabella had always treated her brother’s word as fact. But after hearing their mother’s explanation, the story made an uncomfortable amount of sense.","\"You’re lying to me, aren’t you?\"","\"Get in the car.\"","He guided her into the passenger seat and closed the door. Then he locked it.","Isabella pounded on the window. When he ignored her, she started calling his phone repeatedly.","Alpha Sebastian silenced the calls and kept his eyes on the pier exit. He waited for one particular person to appear.","The crowd slowly thinned.","Eira never came.","She must have already left.","Disappointment flickered across his face before he got into the driver’s seat.","\"Sebastian.\" Isabella refused to drop the subject. \"Is it true? Did you spend all your money on Serena? \"","He knew his sister. Once she got hold of a question, she would not let it go.","Their parents already knew about the money, so denying it would not change anything. Still, he avoided giving her the full truth. Isabella could not keep a secret to save her life.","\"Some of it was an investment,\" he said. \"The rest was a loan.\"","\"A loan?\" Isabella accepted the explanation immediately, but it only made her angrier. \"You had money to lend Serena, but not enough to support your own family?\"","She grabbed the door handle.","\"No way. I’m going to find Serena and get every last dollar back.\""]}]);
